window.LUNA_CHAPTERS=(window.LUNA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":26,"title":"Chapter 26 A Different Plan","paragraphs":["Eira answered before Beatrice could.","\"I was the only one of Dr. Thorne’s students who stopped after a master’s. Everyone else went on to finish a PhD.\"","Beatrice shook her head.","If Alaric had heard that, he would have launched into a twenty-minute lecture about degrees being credentials, not proof of intelligence.","Alpha Killian did not look convinced.","\"That still doesn’t explain the administrative job,\" he said.","\"It explains enough for tonight,\" Beatrice replied.","Her tone stayed pleasant, but the conversation was over.","Alpha Killian understood the boundary and did not push. He watched Eira get into the town car, taking the unanswered question with her.","--","As the car pulled away from Sterling Tower, Beatrice glanced at Alpha Killian and Lila through the rear window.","\"How did you end up with the Sterlings?\"","\"Lila and I became friends.\"","\"She’s easy to like. Professor Chase complains that she talks through his lectures and treats deadlines like suggestions, but he thinks highly of her.\"","Beatrice glanced at Eira. \"And her brother?\"","\"Killian is my boss.\"","\"That’s not what I asked.\"","\"It’s the answer you’re getting.\"","Beatrice’s mouth twitched. \"Fair enough. Killian keeps his cards close. Make sure you keep yours closer.\"","\"There’s nothing between us.\"","\"I didn’t say there was.\"","Eira looked out the window. \"I was Dr. Thorne’s weakest student anyway.\"","Beatrice’s expression softened. \"You were the only one he trusted to work alone.\"","Eira said nothing.","\"You’ve lost weight. Have you been eating?\"","\"Enough.\"","\"That means no.\"","Beatrice reached over and took her hand.","\"I don’t love Sebastian anymore,\" Eira said.","\"I know.\" Beatrice squeezed her fingers. \"But the Pack Court still gives him time to challenge the separation. Has Susan confirmed the filing?\"","\"Yes. If he doesn’t object before the deadline, it becomes final.\"","\"And if he finds out?\"","\"He’ll fight it. He doesn’t want the marriage. He wants what I do for his family.\"","The household. The Pack work. The endless favors.","Serena got the love story. Eira got the labor.","\"I’m not letting him keep both,\" Eira said. \"I’m going back to the Hale estate tomorrow.\"","\"Alone?\"","\"Not to ask permission.\"","Eira looked at Beatrice.","\"Roger and Margaret care about the Hale name, the family trust, and their standing. Once they realize keeping me in this marriage is riskier than letting it end, they’ll pressure Sebastian themselves.\"","Beatrice gave her hand another squeeze.","\"Good. Then make them choose what they care about more.\"","--","When Eira arrived at the Hale estate the next morning, she heard Isabella before she reached the front door.","\"This was supposed to be my birthday weekend!\"","Eira stepped inside.","Isabella stood in the living room with an ice pack pressed to her swollen cheek. Torn wrapping paper, flower samples, and a canceled catering order covered the coffee table.","The birthday party had been called off.","Apparently, that was a tragedy on the level of a natural disaster.","Isabella saw Eira and pointed at her.","\"You.\"","Luna Margaret rose from the sofa. \"You have some nerve walking back into this house.\"","Alpha Roger stood near the fireplace, his expression cold.","\"You struck a member of this Pack in public.\"","\"She shoved Lila first,\" Eira said.","\"Lila Sterling,\" Isabella snapped. \"You could’ve told me who she was.\"","Eira looked at her.","\"You shouldn’t need someone’s family name before deciding not to treat them like trash.\"","Isabella’s face reddened around the swelling.","\"This is your fault. My birthday is ruined.\"","\"No,\" Eira said. \"Your behavior ruined it.\"","Isabella opened her mouth to scream again. \"Enough. Go upstairs.\"","\"But Dad...\"","\"Now.\"","Isabella stormed away, muttering about lawsuits, ruined photos, and how no one in the family ever took her side.","Luna Margaret waited until the bedroom door slammed upstairs. \"What do you want?\"","\"A private conversation.\"","Alpha Roger studied her for a moment, then nodded toward the study.","The study door clicked shut behind them.","Alpha Roger closed the door and turned back to her. \"What do you want?\"","\"A legal separation from Sebastian.\"","Luna Margaret stared at her, then gave a short laugh. \"You’re serious.\"","\"Completely.\"","Alpha Roger studied Eira across the desk. \"Is there someone else?\"","Luna Margaret’s brief amusement vanished.","\"That Sterling Wolf,\" she said. \"Is this about him?\"","\"No.\"","\"Good,\" Alpha Roger said coldly. \"Killian Sterling has his pick of every unmated she-wolf on the West Coast. He wouldn’t risk his name over you.\"","The insult barely registered.","\"I’m leaving the Luna position open for Serena,\" Eira said. \"Isn’t that what this family has wanted from the beginning?\"","Alpha Roger and Luna Margaret exchanged a look.","Serena had the bloodline, the wolf, and the Winthrop connections they valued. Eira had none of those things.","Still, letting Eira leave was different from pushing her aside.","She knew the Hale accounts, Pack vendors, family schedules, and internal records. Worse, she now worked inside Sterling Group.","Luna Margaret’s eyes narrowed.","\"You expect us to let you walk into Sterling territory carrying four years of Hale Pack business?\"","\"I’m not carrying anything. \"Eira placed a folder on Alpha Roger’s desk.","\"The first section is a confidentiality agreement. It covers Pack finances, vendors, internal schedules, private correspondence, and every family matter I handled while I was Luna.\"","Alpha Roger finally opened the folder.","Behind the confidentiality terms sat a complete list of Pack credentials, account access, keys, and records Eira would return when the separation became final.","\"You came prepared,\" he said.","\"I knew what you’d care about.\"","Luna Margaret’s mouth tightened. \"And what exactly are you taking?\"","\"The apartment Sebastian already transferred to me. Nothing from Hale Group. No shares. No bonuses. No claim against future income or the Hale family trust.\"","Luna Margaret leaned over Alpha Roger’s shoulder and scanned the pages.","\"That’s all?\"","\"I’m not here for his money.\"","\"Then why are you here?\" Alpha Roger asked.","\"Because Sebastian has already signed the separation agreement.\"","Luna Margaret’s face brightened.","Then Eira added, \"He doesn’t know he signed it.\"","The room went still.","Alpha Roger looked up. \"You hid the separation terms in the property agreement?\"","\"I gave him a complete contract. The terms were clear. He signed every page without reading them.\"","She tapped the final pages.","\"The filing is already with Pack Court. The thirty-day objection period is running. I need the Hale registrar to process it normally. No private warning to Sebastian. No family challenge.\"","\"You want us to keep this from our son?\" Luna Margaret asked.","\"I want you to protect the Hale Pack.\"","Eira opened the confidentiality section.","\"I’m waiving every financial claim beyond the apartment. I’ll keep your Pack business private. A quiet separation costs you nothing.\"","She tapped the filing papers.","\"If Sebastian challenges it, the court record will include his hidden marriage, Serena living in the marital home, and Isabella’s attack on Sterling Pack’s people. That will become a Hale Pack problem, not just a family problem.\"","Alpha Roger’s expression hardened. \"You’re threatening us.\"","\"I’m offering you the cleanest way out.\"","No one spoke for several seconds.","Finally, Alpha Roger closed the folder. \"We still don’t approve of the way you handled this.\"","\"You don’t need to approve. You only need to stay out of the filing.\"","For several seconds, no one moved.","Then Alpha Roger gave one short nod.","\"Fine.\"","\"One more thing,\" Eira said. \"Isabella cannot know.\"","Luna Margaret glanced toward the closed door. Isabella was already shouting at someone in the hallway about her canceled birthday plans.","\"Especially Isabella.\""]},{"number":27,"title":"Chapter 27 The Dress and the Decision","paragraphs":["The study door swung open.","Isabella, who had been listening with her ear pressed to it, stumbled into the hallway. She caught herself against the doorframe and glared at Eira.","\"Mom. Dad.\" She grabbed Luna Margaret’s arm. \"I thought you were going to do something about her.\"","\"That’s enough, Isabella.\" Luna Margaret patted her hand, then turned to Eira with a careful smile. \"You’re leaving already?\"","Eira slipped on her shoes.","\"I’ve said what I came to say.\"","She picked up her bag and walked out.","Isabella watched her go, confused. Something had happened in that study. Her parents had been furious when Eira arrived. Now they were acting almost polite.","That was not supposed to happen.","Eira was supposed to leave ashamed, not walk out looking like she had just won a negotiation.","Isabella waited until the front door closed. Then she pulled out her phone.","Isabella: Serena, come over tonight. We’re having dinner. Sebastian will be here.","She switched to her brother’s messages.","Isabella: Seb, Serena’s coming over tonight. We can still salvage my birthday dinner. Don’t let Eira ruin everything.","The replies came within minutes.","Serena: I’ll be there.","Sebastian: I’ll come by after work.","Isabella smiled.","Perfect.","She hurried back into the living room.","\"Serena’s coming tonight,\" she announced. \"And Eira is not invited.\"","Luna Margaret guided her back onto the sofa and pressed the ice pack against her cheek.","\"She won’t be coming back tonight,\" Luna Margaret said. \"Let her cool off somewhere else.\"","Isabella’s smile turned smug.","\"Good. Serena can finally have the seat she deserves.\"","Luna Margaret glanced at her. \"Don’t get ahead of yourself.\"","--","At the Thorne estate, Beatrice rested in a lounge chair in the garden, eyes closed as she enjoyed the late-afternoon sun.","She heard footsteps on the path.","\"You’re back,\" she said without opening her eyes.","\"I’m back.\"","Eira knelt beside her and rested her head near Beatrice’s shoulder.","Beatrice heard the exhaustion in her voice. She opened her eyes and smoothed Eira’s hair.","\"I have something for you. Martin, bring it out.\"","Martin Cole appeared a moment later, pushing a dress form across the lawn. An ivory gown hung from it.","The bodice was covered in detailed lace over sheer illusion netting. It showed just enough skin to look elegant, never too much. A high lace collar framed the neckline, and three-dimensional flowers spread across the shoulders and chest.","The skirt was made of heavy satin. The front was simple. The back fell into layered pleats and large satin bows. Long gloves trimmed with pearls completed the look.","The gown looked like something from an old Hollywood romance.","\"It’s from the late nineteenth century,\" Martin explained. \"Dr. Thorne bought it for Mrs. Thorne at auction years ago. She wore it twice. It has been kept in storage ever since. I had a specialist restore it last month. It’s in excellent condition.\"","Eira stared at the dress.","\"For me?\"","\"Do you like it?\" Beatrice stood and walked over to the dress form. She ran her fingers over the lace, her expression softening with memory.","\"Why are you giving me a gown?\"","\"For the gala.\" Beatrice looked at her. \"You never buy formal clothes for yourself. Most modern gowns show more skin than you’d like, and you always end up choosing something plain.\"","She squeezed Eira’s hand.","\"I want you to take care of yourself now. This is the start of a new Chapter.\"","Eira’s throat tightened.","\"Thank you.\"","\"Don’t be silly. Alaric would roll his eyes if he heard you thanking me for a dress.\" Beatrice gave her arm a light tap. \"Now tell me. How did it go with Roger and Margaret?\"","\"They agreed to help with the filing.\"","\"Good.\" Beatrice’s face hardened. \"I’ve waited a long time for you to walk away from that family. After Alaric died, I was so lost in grief that I didn’t see how deeply Sebastian had pulled you into their life.\"","Eira stayed quiet.","\"Though, to be fair, he wasn’t always like this.\" Beatrice’s voice softened. \"He was handsome, attentive, and charming. I can’t blame you for falling for him.\"","She gave a small, amused smile.","\"I fell for Alaric the same way. One look at that face and that calm voice, and I was finished.\"","Eira smiled. \"Did he know?\"","\"Of course. I told him.\" Beatrice’s eyes sparkled. \"I walked up to him and said, ’You’re ridiculously handsome. You should marry me.’\"","Eira laughed.","\"That worked?\"","\"It took him a week to answer. But he did.\"","They spent the rest of the afternoon in the garden, talking until Eira finally felt some of the tension leave her body.","After dinner, she went to her room.","The room was spacious and bright, filled with the small comforts Beatrice had added over the years. Eira opened the top drawer of her desk and took out a black-and-gold envelope.","Her phone rang.","\"Professor Davies.\"","\"Did you get the invitation?\"","\"I did.\" Eira opened the envelope. Her name was printed across the card in elegant gold lettering.","\"You’re going, right?\" Professor Davies asked. \"Only three people received the black-and-gold invitations. Dr. Victor Winthrop, me, and you. Victor won’t attend. His granddaughter Serena is expected to attend in his place.\"","He paused.","\"I’m bringing Claire. She keeps asking if you’ll be there. She says she won’t go unless you do. She gets nervous at these events unless someone she trusts is there.\"","\"I’ll be there.\"","\"Really? You’re not just saying that to make Claire feel better?\"","\"Beatrice wants me to go.\"","\"Then that settles it. If Mrs. Thorne wants you there, I’m satisfied.\"","He hesitated.","\"One more thing. Sebastian will be there. Killian Sterling too, obviously. Be careful.\"","\"I know.\"","Eira looked down at the invitation.","\"Professor Davies.\"","\"Yeah?\"","\"Sebastian isn’t my husband anymore.\"","Silence filled the line.","Then he said quietly, \"I see. I’m sorry, Eira.\"","\"Good night, Professor.\"","\"Good night.\"","The call ended.","Professor Davies lowered his phone and let out a long breath.","\"Finally,\" he murmured. \"She’s finally free.\"","He had watched Eira wear herself down for four years. She skipped meals, ran between the lab and the Hale estate, and lived like an unpaid housekeeper for people who treated her like staff.","It had broken his heart.","If Eira had been his daughter, he would have lost his mind.","Alaric had trusted him to look after her. Eira was like a second daughter to him. But she had seemed content, so he had stayed quiet.","Not anymore.","She was out.","And that was worth celebrating."]},{"number":28,"title":"Chapter 28 The Birthday Dinner","paragraphs":["Alpha Sebastian got back to the Hale estate after eight.","The moment he stepped inside, Isabella launched into a complaint—something about the party she’d wanted versus the dinner she got.","He slipped off his jacket and held it out without thinking.","No one took it.","For four years, Eira had always been there. She hung it up, asked if he wanted tea, made sure dinner was ready before anyone noticed it needed to be.","Tonight, his arm stayed raised in empty air. One second. Two. Long enough to feel stupid.","Serena watched him from the dining room.","\"I can take that,\" she said.","Alpha Sebastian lowered the jacket himself.","\"You didn’t tell me you were coming.\"","Serena glanced at Isabella, then smiled. \"Isabella invited me. I thought it might cheer her up.\"","\"It does,\" Isabella said quickly. \"Serena came for me. Not you.\"","Alpha Sebastian gave a distracted nod and hung up his own coat.","He sat down across from Serena.","She looked effortless in a dark green dress, like she belonged in the Hale dining room more than Eira ever had.","Alpha Roger lifted his glass. \"To Isabella. And to better days ahead.\"","Glasses clinked.","Serena smiled. \"The tech expo’s next week. A lot of attention on the processor launch. Companies ready to support the rollout will have opportunities.\"","Alpha Roger leaned forward. \"Hale Group could be one of them.\"","\"I’m not saying anything specific,\" Serena said lightly. \"Just that it pays to be ready.\"","Luna Margaret’s eyes brightened. Alpha Sebastian watched Serena, but his attention kept sliding back to his phone.","Eira hadn’t come home. Hadn’t called. Hadn’t even sent one of her careful little messages explaining where she was—the ones he’d spent four years half-ignoring and only now noticed the absence of.","He opened their conversation.","Sebastian: Why didn’t you come tonight?","Nothing.","Sebastian: You knew it was Isabella’s birthday.","A reply came a full minute later.","Eira: Mrs. Thorne’s doctor came by. I couldn’t leave.","That was all. No apology. No promise to make it up. No question about whether he’d eaten.","His jaw tightened. He typed, deleted, typed again.","Sebastian: Are you with Sterling right now?","The word Sterling sat on the screen a second before he sent it. He told himself it was about the job. It wasn’t, and some part of him knew it.","Delivered. No reply.","He watched the screen until it dimmed, then locked it too hard.","\"Sebastian?\" Serena’s voice pulled him up. \"You’ve checked that phone six times.\"","\"Work.\"","\"Mm.\" She didn’t argue. She just let the silence say she didn’t believe him, which was worse.","Dinner moved on without him. The wine was too warm. One of Alpha Roger’s preferred dishes was missing. The staff had forgotten Isabella’s birthday candles. Small things. Eira’s things. No one said her name, but the whole table felt the shape of the gap she’d left.","\"So.\" Isabella broke it, bright and pointed. \"The Sterling mixer next week. You’re going, right?\"","\"I am.\"","\"Who are you bringing?\" Serena tilted her head. \"Those nights are always easier with a plus-one.\"","\"Obviously Serena,\" Isabella said, before he could answer. \"Who else? Eira would hate it. She doesn’t know anyone. She’d stand against the wall all night looking miserable.\" She turned to him. \"You’re the Alpha of Hale Pack. You need someone who can work a room.\"","Alpha Sebastian had assumed Eira would be there. Not because he’d planned to introduce her—because she always handled the parts he didn’t want to think about. The right names. The right files. The right answers, before he knew to ask.","Instead she’d be there for Sterling. Sitting at Alpha Killian’s table. Wearing whatever Alpha Killian had bought for the night.","\"She’ll be there,\" he said. \"With Sterling.\"","The table went quiet.","\"With Sterling Group,\" Luna Margaret corrected gently, watching her son. \"She works for them. That’s all that means, Sebastian.\"","\"That’s all it means.\" He heard how flat it came out. So did everyone else.","Serena set her fork down, delicate. \"You know, it’s funny. My grandfather’s been to every one of these. Alpha Killian comes alone. Every year. And the year before.\" She let it breathe. \"I only mention it because people will notice if he changes the habit. For her.\"","Something moved across Alpha Sebastian’s face before he could stop it.","Serena saw it. She’d been fishing for exactly that, and she’d caught it clean.","\"But I’m sure it’s nothing,\" she added sweetly.","\"It’s nothing.\" He said it too fast. His hand had closed around his water glass hard enough to whiten the knuckles, and he made himself let go.","Alpha Roger and Luna Margaret exchanged a look. Isabella, for once, said nothing—just watched her brother realize, a beat too late, that he’d shown the whole table something he’d meant to keep off his own face.","Serena moved in to cover for him, gracious, the picture of understanding. \"Anyway. I have my own invitation—I can go on my own. And Isabella should come. A room full of Pack heirs is good for her.\"","\"Take your sister,\" Luna Margaret said, relieved to change lanes. \"It’s a good opportunity.\"","Alpha Sebastian nodded, distracted. \"All right.\"","Serena waited a beat. Then, light as a feather dropped on purpose: \"So you’ve got your date. Does that mean I can bring someone? A guy I’ve been seeing—it’d be nice to introduce him.\"","The question landed soft. Everyone at the table heard the test underneath it.","She wasn’t seeing anyone. She just wanted to see his face.","\"Sebastian?\"","He looked up.","\"No.\"","It came out before thought did—clipped, fast, too much weight on one syllable. The kind of no that answers a question no one had actually asked yet.","For a second he heard it too. So did his mother. So did Serena, whose eyes warmed with quiet triumph she was careful to fold away.","\"No?\" she echoed, gentle.","He reached for the correction and couldn’t find one that sounded like indifference. \"It’s a business event. Keep it professional.\"","\"Of course.\" Serena lowered her lashes, hiding a smile. \"Good.\"","Across the table, his phone lit up face-down. He turned it over before he could stop himself.","Not Eira.","He set it back down, and this time everyone pretended not to watch him do it."]},{"number":29,"title":"Chapter 29 The Discarded Clothes","paragraphs":["Serena’s smile widened.","The answer pleased her. Alpha Sebastian did not like the idea of her arriving with another man. She filed that away.","\"Then I guess I’ll go alone.\"","\"Not a chance,\" Isabella said brightly. \"Once we’re inside, I’ll give Sebastian right back to you. I won’t be in the way.\"","Serena laughed.","\"You’d better remember that.\"","Alpha Roger and Luna Margaret exchanged a look, then excused themselves for the night. Isabella followed them into the hall.","Before the door closed, she lifted her phone.","Alpha Sebastian had leaned toward Serena after she complained something was in her eye. Serena tipped up her chin and kissed him.","Isabella snapped the photo.","Perfect.","She sent it to Eira.","Isabella: Thought you should see this. He looks happier with Serena. Stop pretending your marriage has a future.","Eira’s phone was still switched off. The message sat unread.","--","Alpha Sebastian pulled back first.","\"Serena.\"","He glanced toward the closed dining room door.","\"We should probably be careful.\"","\"Is it wrong?\" Serena asked softly. \"You care about me. I care about you.\"","\"No.\" The answer came too fast. \"It’s not wrong.\"","Serena smiled but gave him space.","\"I’m tired. Can you show me to my room?\"","\"Of course.\"","She held out her hand.","\"I’m still a little dizzy.\"","Alpha Sebastian took it and led her down the hall.","At the guest suite, Serena glanced at the door beside it.","\"Your room is next door?\"","\"It is.\" He stopped at the threshold. \"If you need anything, call me.\"","\"I need something now.\" Her smile was small. \"Something to sleep in.\"","\"Give me a minute.\"","Alpha Sebastian went to his room and opened the closet.","His shirts hung neatly on one side. Eira’s clothes filled the other.","Plain white T-shirts. Cotton shorts. Soft, practical things bought for comfort, not attention.","She had bought them in multipacks, always choosing the cheapest option.","He had told her more than once to buy something nicer. Silk pajamas, maybe. Something that looked less like it came from a clearance bin.","She always said the old shirts worked fine.","His phone was still in his hand.","He opened his messages.","Sebastian: I’m clearing some space in the closet. You should replace the old sleepwear when you can.","The message stayed undelivered.","No argument. No question.","He gathered several of Eira’s shirts and dropped them into a storage bag.","A tie pin caught the light on the shelf above.","Eira had picked it out. The tie beside it, too. His watch. His briefcase. Half the things that made him look successful had passed through her hands.","Then there were her clothes. Cheap cotton. Barely taking up space.","The contrast sat badly with him.","\"Sebastian?\"","Serena stood in the doorway, one hand on the frame.","\"It’s taking you forever to find one shirt.\"","He reached for one of his own button-downs.","\"Nothing in here will fit you comfortably. Take this.\"","She accepted it, then glanced at the trash bin.","\"What’s that?\"","\"Nothing.\"","Serena looked at the white shirts.","\"You don’t have to keep a museum of a marriage that’s already ending,\" she said gently.","Alpha Sebastian’s eyes moved back to the bin. \"I’ll deal with it later.\"","\"Of course.\"","--","At Beatrice’s estate, Eira turned her phone back on before bed.","Notifications flooded the screen.","Beatrice’s missed calls. Alpha Sebastian’s undelivered messages. Then Isabella’s photo.","Alpha Sebastian and Serena kissing on the couch.","So what?","Serena’s perfume had already been in Eira’s bedroom. Black lace had already been under the bed. The sheets had told the rest of the story.","Then she saw Alpha Sebastian’s message.","[I’m clearing some space in the closet. You should replace the old sleepwear when you can.]","Fine.","She had not planned to go back for those clothes anyway.","She scrolled through old messages with Alpha Sebastian.","The last two weeks were almost empty.","Further back, they were full of small reminders.","Eira: What do you want for dinner?","Eira: Your gray suit is pressed.","Eira: Your tie clip is on the dresser.","His replies never changed.","Sebastian: Thanks, wife.","The word used to make her feel chosen.","Now it looked like an automatic response from a man who had never really seen her.","She locked the phone and turned over.","Sleep came late.","--","The Thorne kitchen was quiet the next morning.","The housekeeper looked up when Eira walked in.","\"Miss Crawford, are you hungry? I can make breakfast.\"","\"I’ve got it,\" Eira said. \"Thank you.\"","She made a batch of breakfast biscuits with eggs, sausage, and sharp cheddar.","At the group home, a hot biscuit had once felt like a real luxury. It was simple, filling, and warm enough to make a bad morning survivable.","By the time she finished, a tray of oversized biscuit sandwiches sat on the counter.","The housekeeper stared.","\"They’re huge.\"","\"That’s the point.\"","For Alpha Sebastian, she had learned to make tiny, careful things. Mini quiches. Small pastries. Food that looked good on a polished table.","But this was what she liked.","She left a few for Beatrice and the staff, packed the rest, and headed to Sterling Tower.","At work, Eira set one wrapped biscuit on Natalie’s desk.","Natalie looked at it.","\"Breakfast.\"","\"You made breakfast for me?\"","\"I made too many.\"","Natalie took a bite.","Then stopped.","\"Oh, wow.\"","\"Apparently, something worth stealing,\" Natalie said, pulling the bag closer.","Eira handed Kate one too.","Miles arrived a few minutes later. Natalie held out the last extra biscuit.","\"You want one?\"","\"What is?\"","Alpha Killian’s voice cut through the room.","Miles turned. \"Miss Crawford brought in homemade breakfast biscuits.\"","Alpha Killian looked toward Eira’s bag.","Only one remained. The one Eira had set aside for herself.","\"Let me try one.\"","Eira moved before anyone else could.","She grabbed the last biscuit and took a large bite.","\"Sorry, Alpha Killian,\" she said around the mouthful. \"Last one.\"","The office went quiet for half a second.","Then Natalie looked down at her desk to hide a smile."]},{"number":30,"title":"Chapter 30 Red Ink","paragraphs":["Alpha Killian passed Eira’s desk and glanced at the biscuit in her hand.","\"Eating that fast? Careful you don’t choke.\"","\"Thanks for your concern, Alpha Killian.\"","Eira swallowed, then deliberately took another large bite.","A second later, the dry biscuit caught in her throat.","She coughed sharply. Miles set a bottle of water on her desk before she could reach for one, while Natalie gave her back a quick pat.","Alpha Killian stopped.","Eira drank some water and looked at him over the bottle.","\"I’ll add it to my training plan.\"","The corner of his mouth almost moved.","\"Good.\"","Alpha Killian returned to his office, with Miles following to deliver the morning briefing. A few minutes later, Miles came back out and closed the door behind him.","Natalie waited until he had passed. \"Can I ask you something personal?\"","\"You can ask.\"","\"That man we saw the other day at the mall,\" Kate said slowly. \"Alpha Sebastian from Hale Group. That’s your husband?\"","She still could not quite believe it.","\"We’ve been with Alpha Killian for years,\" Natalie added. \"We know most of the Alphas in the major packs around Palo Alto. We even—\"","Kate lowered her voice. \"We even know which Alphas are keeping which mistresses. But we never heard a whisper that Alpha Sebastian was married.\"","\"That’s normal.\" Eira took smaller bites now, speaking calmly. \"He and I never appeared together in public.\"","Kate blinked. \"Did you at least have a ceremony?\"","Eira hesitated.","Natalie reached over and lightly touched Kate’s arm. Kate pressed her lips together. She realized she had overstepped.","Eira saw their expressions shift. \"We did. It was a pretty lively event.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s family had been there. So had his packmates.","Natalie and Kate became more certain something was very wrong. They said nothing more. Neither of them brought up what they had noticed at the mall that day.","Alpha Sebastian and that woman had smelled the same. Either they wore the same perfume, or they had been close enough for the scent to transfer.","\"Eira,\" Natalie said carefully. \"Just one more question. Please don’t be upset.\"","She took a quick sip of water.","\"If Alpha Sebastian had a ceremony with you, why doesn’t he bring you to events? Is it because you’re not available? You don’t have to answer if—\"","\"It’s because he thinks I’m not suitable,\" Eira said.","Some things only became easier to move past once they were said out loud.","Kate’s face darkened. \"Not suitable? You’re his wife. Who’s more suitable than that? That woman from the mall?\"","Natalie bit her lip.","Kate, you are brave.","Eira nodded and returned to her desk. She opened her weekly and daily reports and began typing.","Natalie and Kate wisely said nothing more.","--","By lunch, Eira got a call from the front desk.","Her new phone had arrived.","She told them to hold it until the end of the day. She still had work to finish.","Late that afternoon, Miles stepped into the executive office carrying three slim black Sterling Group cases.","Kate looked up first.","\"Please tell me those aren’t more spreadsheets.\"","\"Expo kits,\" Miles said. \"For the executive event team.\"","He handed one case to Natalie, one to Kate, and one to Eira.","\"Secure work phone. Charger. Encrypted badge holder. Event access pass.\" He looked at them over his glasses. \"Use the phones during the expo. Keep them charged. Don’t lose them.\"","Kate opened hers.","\"Okay. This is actually kind of nice.\"","Natalie checked the event pass. \"And the phone?\"","\"Required for the show floor and evening mixer,\" Miles said. \"The event network runs through Sterling security.\"","Eira opened her case.","Inside was a new white phone, a security case, and a slim charger.","The same model she had ordered that morning.","Only this one was for work.","\"I already bought a phone,\" she said.","Miles nodded. \"Then you’ll have a personal phone and a company phone. This one stays with you during the expo.\"","Reasonable.","Too reasonable.","\"Okay. Corporate finally did something I respect.\"","Natalie checked the event pass. \"We should thank Alpha Killian. He approved the budget.\"","Miles looked up as they approached.","\"Can we see Alpha Killian for a second?\" Natalie asked. \"Just to thank him for approving the expo package.\"","Miles knocked once, then opened the door.","Alpha Killian looked up from his laptop.","Kate stepped in first.","\"Thank you for the event budget,\" she said. \"We’ll make the executive team look good.\"","Natalie held up her secure phone. \"And we’ll keep the tech charged. Promise.\"","Alpha Killian gave a short nod. \"See that you do.\"","\"Miss Crawford. Stay.\"","Natalie and Kate exchanged a quick look.","\"We’ll save you a seat at lunch,\" Natalie said.","The two women left with their cases. Miles followed them out.","The office door closed behind Eira.","\"Alpha Killian.\"","Eira paused at the door.","\"Come look at this.\" He held out a document and his pen. \"Tell me if anything jumps out.\"","She took the document first.","A bid proposal. Her stomach dropped.","Then she saw the project name. Not the Sovereign Processor Initiative. Not hers.","She let out a quiet breath. \"What am I looking for?\"","\"Anything that doesn’t hold up.\"","\"It’s lunch.\"","\"Read first.\"","Of course.","Bosses always found a way to turn a five-minute favor into unpaid overtime.","Eira sighed and took the pen.","The first pages were standard. Then the numbers started drifting.","A delivery estimate in one section did not match the projected volume in another. A cost assumption came from an outdated market report. The risk section treated supply delays like a minor inconvenience.","She circled one line. Then another.","By the last page, the paper was covered in red ink.","\"Done.\"","Alpha Killian picked up the document.","\"Your volume forecast is too low. The delivery schedule doesn’t support the demand model, and the risk section is pretending supply delays won’t matter.\" Eira tapped the final page. \"They will.\"","Alpha Killian’s brow tightened. He called Miles.","\"Tell the project team there’s an emergency meeting at one-thirty. Full review. No exceptions.\"","He ended the call and looked at Eira. \"First Lila’s thesis. Now this.\"","\"I went to school.\"","\"That answer is doing a lot of work.\"","\"It’s still the answer.\"","For a moment, neither of them moved.","Then Alpha Killian gestured toward the door. \"Go eat.\"","Back upstairs, she ate at her desk while transferring her contacts and photos to the new black device. The white Sterling phone remained unopened beside it.","At one twenty-five, Miles stopped at her desk.","\"Conference room. Project review.\"","Eira looked at her half-finished lunch.","\"Already?\"","\"Your notes started it.\""]},{"number":31,"title":"Chapter 31 The Data Doesn’t Lie","paragraphs":["Inside the conference room, Eira saw what real authority looked like.","Alpha Killian placed the marked proposal on the table and looked at the project team.","The proposal moved around the table.","The room went silent.","One by one, the project leads found Eira’s red circles and notes. Their expressions tightened.","Alpha Killian waited until everyone had read them.","\"You missed these,\" he said. \"An outside auditor won’t.\"","The project director cleared his throat. \"We’ll revise the proposal immediately, Alpha Killian.\"","\"Do it here.\" Alpha Killian tapped the document once. \"Now.\"","No one argued.","The team opened their laptops and got to work.","Eira sat at the side table with Natalie and Kate. Natalie tracked action items while Kate updated the deadline sheet. Eira followed the discussion, comparing each revised section with the original proposal.","Twenty minutes later, a new spreadsheet appeared on the screen.","Something still looked wrong.","Eira checked the source column, then checked it again.","\"That figure still doesn’t work,\" she said.","Every head turned toward her.","Alpha Killian looked up. \"Why?\"","\"The result doesn’t match the input.\" Eira pointed at the screen. \"This row uses the current demand forecast, but that number came from an older data set.\"","The project manager frowned. \"That’s the figure in the system.\"","\"Then the system is pulling from the wrong source.\"","A quiet tension moved through the room.","That did not automatically mean someone had changed the data. It could be an old file, a bad link, or a simple entry error.","But any of those could damage the bid.","The manager leaned back. \"With respect, Miss Crawford, you joined the executive office this week. Our analysts have been working on this project for months.\"","Alpha Killian’s voice cut in. \"And they still missed the errors that brought everyone into this room.\"","The manager stopped.","Alpha Killian looked at Eira. \"Can you trace the source?\"","\"I can try.\"","He turned to one of the analysts. \"Give her access to the source log.\"","The analyst entered a temporary access code on Eira’s laptop.","Alpha Killian turned back to the team.","\"The rest of you keep working. We’re not leaving this room until the numbers match.\"","The room filled with keyboard clicks.","Eira connected the spreadsheet to the source log. A few minutes later, she found the problem.","\"This forecast is linked to last quarter’s database snapshot.\"","The project director checked the file path and swore under his breath. \"She’s right.\"","Alpha Killian’s expression did not change. \"Fix the link. Rebuild the model. I want the corrected proposal by five.\"","\"Yes, Alpha Killian.\"","Alpha Killian stood and gathered his files. At the door, he looked at Eira. \"Miss Crawford. Back to the executive floor.\"","She picked up her tablet and followed.","The second the door closed, voices rose behind them.","\"Who is she?\"","\"Her name sat in Administrative Support for years, but I don’t remember ever seeing her.\"","\"And now she’s working directly for Alpha Killian?\"","--","Back at her desk, Eira finished setting up her new personal phone.","The white Sterling-issued device sat beside it, still in the box.","Kate nodded toward it. \"You know that thing has a full terabyte, right?\"","\"It’s for work.\"","\"I could fill a terabyte by Friday.\"","Natalie glanced over her monitor. \"That is not the flex you think it is.\"","While they argued, Eira’s old photo library continued syncing.","Hundreds of pictures became thousands.","Breakfasts. Dinners. Carefully plated meals built around Alpha Sebastian’s schedule, his diet, and whatever he happened to want that day.","Kate leaned closer. \"You made all of those?\"","\"Yes.\"","Eira opened the largest album.","SEBASTIAN","More than two thousand photos.","She stared at the album for a moment, then stopped the transfer.","Kate glanced at her. \"Having second thoughts?\"","\"Not anymore.\"","Eira deleted the album. Then she cleared it from Recently Deleted.","Next came the contacts she had saved for Alpha Sebastian. His tailor. His dry cleaner. Hale Pack vendors. Relatives who only called when they needed something fixed.","One by one, she removed them.","When she finished, the new phone looked almost empty.","It did not feel like losing four years.","It felt like taking back the space.","She powered off the old phone and put it in her desk drawer.","Kate watched the whole thing. \"That was either extremely healthy or the first five minutes of a revenge movie.\"","\"Could be both.\"","Natalie nodded. \"Either way, I support it.\"","The Sterling phone chimed.","Miles had added Eira to Sterling Secure, the company’s encrypted workspace for executive staff and Pack leadership.","The first channel appeared automatically.","Executive Operations","Five members: Alpha Killian, Miles, Natalie, Kate, and Eira.","A second invitation arrived a second later.","Executive Survival Guide","Four members.","No Alpha.","Eira looked at Kate.","\"Don’t ask,\" Kate said.","Natalie lowered her voice. \"Never leave it open when he walks by.\"","Three rules were pinned at the top.","No screenshots.","Nothing leaves this channel.","If he says \"quick meeting,\" cancel your evening.","A laugh slipped out of Eira.","The lab had given her impossible problems to solve. Hale Pack had given her endless messes to clean up.","This felt different.","Light. Easy. Almost normal.","Natalie pointed at the official channel. \"Send Alpha Killian a quick message so he knows your device is active.\"","\"Is there a standard format?\"","\"I can send you one.\"","Eira had already typed.","Eira: Sterling device is active. Eira Crawford.","Natalie blinked. \"Or that.\"","Kate leaned back in her chair. \"He’ll answer sometime before the next full moon.\"","The phone chimed seven seconds later.","Alpha Killian: Noted. Keep both phones with you.","Silence.","Kate slowly turned toward Natalie.","Natalie checked the time, as if the clock might explain what had just happened.","\"Seven seconds.\"","\"He was probably already online,\" Eira said.","Then she returned to her work.","Her personal phone buzzed.","Alpha Sebastian.","Sebastian: My suit is still at the tailor. Pick it up tonight. I need it for the expo next week.","No please. No mention of the evening mixer. Just another task dropped into her lap because he assumed she would handle it.","For four years, she always had.","Not today.","Eira: I’ll arrange delivery.","She opened the tailor’s website through the order link Alpha Sebastian had sent months ago and called the listed number.","Done.","She returned to work.","Twenty minutes before the end of the day, Alpha Sebastian called.","\"Why didn’t you bring the suit yourself?\"","Eira kept typing. \"Because I was working.\"","\"You could’ve dropped it off on your way home.\"","\"I’m not going home.\"","A beat of silence.","\"You used to bring dinner to my office all the time.\"","That stopped her hands.","She remembered one evening at Hale Group. She had stood near reception with an insulated dinner bag while two employees spoke behind the desk.","\"Alpha Sebastian’s house manager is here again.\"","\"The blonde with the food?\"","\"Yeah. Must be nice. She cooks, runs errands, probably organizes his whole life.\"","\"I thought she was his wife.\"","The other woman had laughed.","\"Please. If Sebastian Hale were married, the whole Bay Area business grapevine would know.\"","Eira had walked away before they noticed her.","At the time, she had told herself it did not matter.","Now she knew better.","No one knew because Alpha Sebastian had made sure they never would."]},{"number":32,"title":"Chapter 32 Terms and Conditions","paragraphs":["The memory faded.","Eira kept her voice even. \"I don’t remember. You stopped coming home for dinner, and you stopped asking me to bring food to the office.\"","That shut Alpha Sebastian up.","He knew exactly where he had been. Since Serena returned, he had picked her up from work almost every night. Dinner with her had become part of his routine.","\"You know how busy I am,\" he said. \"Late meetings. Client dinners.\"","The same excuses, recycled until even he believed them.","\"Next time, pick up the suit yourself,\" Eira said.","His tone softened. \"How’s Mrs. Thorne?\"","\"She’s fine.\"","\"Good. Come home tomorrow. You’re not working this weekend, right?\"","\"No.\"","\"Perfect. I signed you up for something. Check your messages.\"","He hung up before she could ask what he meant.","Four registration notices appeared on her screen.","Preconception Health and Wellness.","Family Planning for Pack Couples.","Newborn Care Basics.","Infant Nutrition and Development.","Two classes on Saturday. Two on Sunday.","Eira stared at the screen.","So this was his gift.","Not a conversation. Not an apology. Not even a question about whether she wanted children.","Just four classes built around a future he had never offered her until she started pulling away.","For four years, Alpha Sebastian had kept her out of his bed and hidden her from the world. Now that she was leaving, he wanted her to imagine a home, a pup, and the real marriage she had once wanted.","He did not need to give her that future.","He only needed her to believe it might happen.","If she believed him, she might quit her job. She might come home. She might start obeying him again.","It was not a promise. It was bait.","Eira closed the messages and returned to her desk.","Natalie was trying to unload a prepaid fitness package she no longer used. Kate had a local resale app open on her phone.","\"Put it on BayPass,\" Kate said. \"I sold a concert ticket there in six minutes.\"","\"What’s BayPass?\" Eira asked.","\"Local tickets, memberships, prepaid classes. Anything the original provider allows you to transfer.\"","Eira looked at the four registration notices Alpha Sebastian had sent.","\"Does that include course packages?\"","\"Usually.\" Kate glanced at her. \"What are you trying to sell?\"","Eira handed her the phone.","Natalie read the class titles and went still.","\"Sebastian signed you up for family-planning classes without asking you?\"","\"All four of them.\"","Kate stared at the weekend schedule.","\"That’s not a gift. That’s a hostage situation with a diaper bag.\"","A reluctant smile tugged at Eira’s mouth.","Natalie did not smile.","\"Are you actually planning to have a pup with him?\"","\"Sebastian wants me to think we are.\"","The answer quieted both women.","Eira opened BayPass.","\"I’m not falling for it.\"","She called the program office before listing the package. The registration was nonrefundable, but the workshops could be transferred once before the first session. Eira was the registered attendee, so only her authorization was required.","That was good enough for her.","She listed all four classes for one hundred dollars.","Natalie leaned over her shoulder.","\"That package cost almost four grand.\"","\"I want it out of my life by tonight.\"","\"Honestly? Fair.\"","An hour later, she found a buyer named Rachel.","The transfer paperwork took less than ten minutes.","Then the program coordinator called.","\"We can transfer the registration electronically, but we still need the serial number from your access badge. It was included in the welcome packet.\"","\"I never received a welcome packet.\"","\"Our records show it was delivered this afternoon to the address provided when Mr. Hale purchased the package.\"","After ending the call, Eira opened her text thread with Sebastian.","Eira: Did the welcome packet for the classes arrive today?","His reply came almost at once.","Sebastian: It’s at our place. Pick it up when you come home.","Not if she came home.","When.","He still thought the classes had worked. One hint about pups and a future together, and he expected her to fall back in line.","Eira typed her response.","Eira: I’ll stop by for the packet.","She would have to visit the apartment that night.","She called the Thorne estate.","Martin answered.","\"I need to stop by the Hale apartment after work,\" Eira said. \"I’m not sure how long it’ll take.\"","\"I can have one of the drivers pick you up.\"","Eira glanced at the time. The driver would have to wait outside while she dealt with Alpha Killian, and there was no telling how long that might take.","\"Thank you, but I’ll find another ride. I don’t want anyone stuck waiting on me all evening.\"","\"Call if your plans change,\" Martin said. \"Mrs. Thorne will worry if you disappear without checking in.\"","\"I will.\"","The moment Eira ended the call, her phone buzzed.","Lila: I’m stopping by Sterling Tower to grab a tablet I left in Alpha Killian’s car. Still at the office?","A second message followed.","Lila: Also, one cup of coffee doesn’t come close to paying you back for saving my thesis. Let me buy you dinner.","Eira: Dinner sounds good. I just need to make one stop first.","Lila: Anywhere fun?","Eira: The Hale apartment. I need to pick up a package.","The typing bubble appeared almost at once.","Lila: Okay, so definitely not fun.","Eira smiled despite herself.","Lila: Take care of it. Text me when you’re done, and I’ll pick you up out front.","Eira: You don’t have to wait around for me.","Lila: I won’t. I’ll be getting tacos and pretending I’m a patient person.","Another message came through.","Lila: Take your time, though. If things get uncomfortable, call me. Dinner can wait.","The quiet concern beneath the joke warmed something in Eira’s chest.","For someone she had known only a few days, Lila was strangely easy to talk to.","Maybe that was because Lila had never asked Eira to earn her kindness first.","--","By the time she finished the transfer paperwork, most of the office had cleared out.","She grabbed her bag and headed toward the elevators.","Miles nearly walked into her as he stepped out of Alpha Killian’s office.","They both stopped.","\"Still here?\" he asked.","\"Personal errand. I lost track of time.\"","Miles nodded and turned back toward the open office door.","\"Compliance flagged another issue with Hale Group’s bid,\" he told Alpha Killian. \"Three hundred thousand dollars a month is being routed through an overseas research foundation, but the actual beneficiary isn’t disclosed in the filings.\"","Eira froze.","She knew those payments.","Alpha Sebastian had called them research support. He had said the money allowed Serena to stay overseas and focus on her work.","Eira turned back.","The office door was still open.","She knocked once.","Alpha Killian looked up from the report in front of him. \"What is it?\"","\"I know who receives the money.\"","Miles glanced at her, then at Alpha Killian.","Alpha Killian leaned back in his chair. \"Come in.\"","Eira entered and closed the door behind her.","\"The payments go to Serena Winthrop,\" she said. \"Sebastian funded her overseas research for years.\"","Alpha Killian’s expression stayed unreadable. \"That’s a serious claim.\"","\"You can verify it.\"","\"And what do you want?\"","\"If the records can legally be released, I want a copy sent to my attorney.\"","Alpha Killian held her gaze.","\"For your separation case.\"","It was not a question.","\"Yes.\""]},{"number":33,"title":"Chapter 33 Cleaning Up His Mess","paragraphs":["Eira reached the apartment building as movers carried the last of Serena’s belongings through the lobby.","Designer boxes crowded two luggage carts. Garment bags, framed artwork, and enough suitcases for a year abroad filled the entrance.","Serena stood near the elevators in four-inch heels, directing traffic.","\"Careful with that,\" she told a mover. \"That bag costs more than your truck.\"","The mover’s jaw tightened, but he kept going.","Then Serena spotted Eira.","\"I wasn’t expecting you tonight.\"","\"I’m here to grab something.\"","Serena glanced at the mountain of boxes and sighed. \"Sorry about the chaos. Alpha Sebastian bought me so much that moving everything into the penthouse has taken all day.\"","Eira looked over the designer luggage. \"Donate half of it.\"","Serena laughed. \"Champagne problems.\"","\"Still sounds like a problem.\"","Her smile tightened.","\"You really don’t care that Alpha Sebastian bought all this for me?\"","\"You got a penthouse, a moving crew, and half of Neiman Marcus.\" Eira met her eyes. \"If you still need my jealousy to enjoy it, he should’ve saved his money.\"","Color rose in Serena’s cheeks.","\"He loves me.\"","\"Then go enjoy the penthouse. Why are you still here pitching it to me?\"","\"Because you’re still in the way.\"","Eira pressed the elevator button. \"Am I?\"","Serena stepped closer. \"If he loves me, then I’m not the other woman. You are.\"","There it was — cheating dressed up as destiny.","Eira stepped into the elevator.","\"That might work better if he weren’t still hiding you from his wife.\"","\"Sebastian is going to divorce you.\"","\"Great.\" Eira faced her as the doors began to close. \"Tell him to stop talking and file.\"","The doors slid shut before Serena could answer.","--","Eira unlocked the apartment with her fingerprint.","The moment she stepped inside, stale takeout and Serena’s perfume hit her at once.","The place looked like the aftermath of a fraternity weekend. A jacket hung over the back of the couch. Empty containers covered the coffee table. A sock lay beside the television. Another had somehow ended up near the kitchen island.","For four years, Eira had cleaned every mess before Alpha Sebastian noticed it existed.","Without her, the whole apartment had fallen apart in less than a week.","She almost picked up the jacket.","Habit pulled at her fingers.","Eira stopped herself.","Not her jacket. Not her mess. Not her problem.","The welcome packet had been delivered to the building’s front desk, but the concierge needed Alpha Sebastian to approve sending it upstairs. Until he returned, Eira had time to collect a few personal things.","She went to the walk-in closet and opened an empty overnight bag.","A few sweaters. Two pairs of jeans. Her spare laptop charger. The framed photograph of her and Beatrice from graduate school.","Nothing Alpha Sebastian would notice right away.","He thought the family-planning classes would bring her home. For now, she wanted him to keep believing that.","People got careless when they thought they were winning.","The front door opened twenty minutes later.","\"Eira?\" Alpha Sebastian sounded surprised. Then pleased.","He found her in the walk-in closet, folding a sweater into her overnight bag. \"You came home.\"","\"I came for the class packet.\"","His smile dimmed. \"Right.\"","His gaze dropped to the open bag. \"What are you doing?\"","\"Packing a few things to take with me.\"","Before he could press her, his attention shifted to the suit draped over a nearby chair—the one that had been delivered to his office.","\"That needs to be steamed before the expo.\"","\"The steamer is in the laundry room.\"","\"You always take care of my suits,\" he said.","\"Then this is a great time for you to learn.\"","\"Eira.\"","\"Sebastian.\" She matched his warning tone so perfectly that his eyes narrowed.","For years, one look from him had been enough to make her drop whatever she was doing and take care of him. Apparently, he had not noticed that those days were over.","He snatched up the suit. \"Fine. I’ll do it.\"","\"I believe in you.\" She turned back to her bag.","Alpha Sebastian walked into the bedroom, muttering under his breath. A moment later, he called, \"The sheets need to be changed.\"","\"Then change them.\"","Silence followed.","Eira stepped out of the closet.","Alpha Sebastian stood beside the bed with the comforter pulled back, staring at a faint stain on the fitted sheet.","A trace of Serena’s perfume lingered beneath the detergent and stale air. So faint that Eira might have missed it if she had not been looking for it.","Alpha Sebastian saw her in the doorway and jerked the comforter back over the bed.","Too late.","\"Problem?\" Eira asked.","\"No.\" His answer came too quickly. \"I was about to wash the sheets.\"","\"Look at you, taking initiative.\"","His eyes searched her face, trying to decide how much she had noticed.","Eira gave him nothing. Let him sweat.","Alpha Sebastian stripped the bed and carried the sheets toward the laundry room.","As he passed her, Eira glanced around the apartment. \"You might want to deal with the rest of this place while you’re at it.\"","He stopped. \"You’re not going to help?\"","\"I didn’t make the mess.\"","\"This is still our home.\"","\"Then you should know how to maintain it.\"","\"You’ve been gone all week,\" he said instead. \"Of course things piled up.\"","\"You run a tech company, Sebastian. I’m sure you can outsmart a washing machine.\"","\"I’ve been busy.\"","\"So have I.\"","That left him with nowhere to go.","He carried the sheets away without another word.","Eira returned to the closet and continued packing while Alpha Sebastian cleaned.","The vacuum started in the living room. Cabinet doors opened and shut. Dishes clattered into the sink.","Then everything went quiet.","Eira paused with a sweater in her hands.","In the living room, Alpha Sebastian had found a tube of deep-red lipstick wedged between the couch cushions.","Eira did not own anything in that shade.","He glanced toward the hallway, then slipped it into his pocket.","A few minutes later, while gathering clothes from the bedroom floor, he spotted a scrap of black lace beneath the bed.","Serena’s underwear.","His face lost all color. He shoved it into his other pocket and checked the floor again, this time on his hands and knees.","Eira watched from the closet doorway.","\"Lose something?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s head snapped up.","\"A cuff link.\"","After that, Alpha Sebastian cleaned like he was erasing a crime scene. He checked beneath the furniture, emptied the trash, and wiped down every surface Serena might have touched.","The intercom buzzed just as he finished.","Alpha Sebastian straightened, breathing harder than a man should after changing a set of sheets.","The concierge’s voice came through the speaker.","\"Mr. Hale, the welcome packet from the family-planning program is downstairs. Would you like us to send it up?\"","\"Yes.\"","A building attendant delivered one large envelope a few minutes later. Inside were four course guides, a transfer form, and four access badges.","Alpha Sebastian handed them to Eira.","\"What do you think?\"","\"It’s thorough.\"","That was all he was getting.","He studied her face, clearly waiting for gratitude. Maybe even tears.","Eira slipped the entire packet into her bag.","\"We can talk about which room to use for a nursery this weekend,\" he said. \"There’s no rush, but it’s good to start planning.\"","There it was. Another carefully measured piece of a future he never intended to give her.","\"Sure,\" Eira said.","Alpha Sebastian relaxed.","He thought she had taken the bait.","Eira took out her phone and sent Lila a single taco emoji. Their signal. She was ready to leave.","Less than ten seconds later, the phone rang.","Eira looked at the screen.","It was not Lila."]},{"number":34,"title":"Chapter 34 The Open Door","paragraphs":["Eira hesitated before answering the call.","\"Hello?\"","\"Come back to the office.\" Alpha Killian’s voice was calm and final. \"We have a last-minute briefing.\"","Eira pulled the phone away and checked the screen.","Alpha Killian.","Before she could respond, Lila’s voice exploded in the background.","\"You have got to be kidding me. I tell you where she is because I’m worried, and you turn it into mandatory overtime? I was supposed to take her out for tacos!\"","\"Thirty minutes,\" Alpha Killian said.","The call ended.","\"What was that about?\" Alpha Sebastian asked.","\"Work.\" Eira slipped her phone into her bag. \"I have to go back to Sterling Tower.\"","Alpha Sebastian checked his watch. \"At this hour?\"","\"Apparently, Alpha Killian doesn’t believe in business hours.\"","That explanation needed no embellishment. Alpha Killian’s reputation did the rest.","Alpha Sebastian’s brow remained furrowed. \"I thought you were resigning.\"","\"The paperwork is still being processed.\" Eira adjusted the strap of her bag. \"Until it’s official, I still work there.\"","It was the answer Alpha Sebastian wanted to hear. His shoulders relaxed.","\"What’s so urgent?\" he asked. \"Does it have something to do with the tech expo? Or the Hale bid?\"","There it was.","He never asked about her work unless he thought it might benefit him.","Eira gave him a mild look. \"I’m an executive assistant, not corporate intelligence.\"","\"I was just asking.\"","\"Then I just answered.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s mouth tightened. For a second, she could almost see him reconsidering how useful she might be inside Sterling.","\"Fine,\" he said. \"Go.\"","Eira reached for the door.","\"Wait.\"","She looked back.","Alpha Sebastian nodded toward the welcome packet inside her bag. \"What do you think of the classes?\"","He was watching her too closely.","This was not a question about the program. He wanted to know if she had taken the bait.","Eira lowered her eyes, playing the part he expected.","\"They look good. And expensive.\" She paused. \"You’ve never spent that much on me before.\"","Guilt flickered across Alpha Sebastian’s face, but it lasted only a second. Satisfaction soon took its place.","\"We’ll talk about our future soon,\" he said.","\"Sure.\"","Eira stepped into the hall and closed the door behind her. The moment she was alone, the smile vanished from her face.","--","She called a ride and headed back to Sterling Tower.","Lila was waiting in the lobby when Eira arrived, holding her car keys in one hand and an iced coffee in the other.","\"Before you say anything, I’m sorry.\" Lila offered her the coffee. \"Killian asked why I was hanging around, so I told him I was waiting for you to leave the Hale apartment. I didn’t expect him to use that information to hijack taco night.\"","Eira accepted the drink. \"You gave me a reason to leave. I’m not complaining.\"","\"Technically, Killian gave you the reason.\" Lila made a face. \"I hate giving him credit. It goes straight to his head.\"","Eira took a sip of coffee. \"Does he know you talk about him like this?\"","\"Constantly. He survives.\"","They crossed the quiet lobby and entered the elevator.","\"Is there actually work to do?\" Eira asked as the doors closed.","\"Probably. Killian would never invent an emergency when he could find a real one.\"","That sounded exactly like him.","When the elevator opened on the executive floor, almost every desk was empty. Only the lights inside Alpha Killian’s office and the nearby conference lounge were still on.","Alpha Killian stood behind his desk with his sleeves rolled to his forearms. A fresh briefing packet lay in front of him.","He did not ask what had happened at the apartment.","Eira did not offer.","\"The expo organizers updated the guest list an hour ago,\" he said. \"Three investors were added, two panelists dropped out, and Hale Group changed its delegation.\"","So there really was work.","Of course there was. Alpha Killian Sterling would never invent an excuse when he could find a real deadline and weaponize it.","He handed her the packet.","\"Review the priority profiles,\" Alpha Killian said. \"Flag any Pack ties, conflicts, or business relationships that could affect the bid. I want the brief on my desk by eight tomorrow morning.\"","Eira flipped through the thick packet. \"All of this tonight?\"","\"No. I printed it so you could admire the page numbers.\"","She looked up. His face remained perfectly serious.","\"Good to know sarcasm is part of the executive training program.\"","A trace of amusement flickered in his eyes.","\"Use the conference lounge. Lila can stay with you.\"","--","The conference lounge sat across from Alpha Killian’s office, with only a glass wall and an open door between them.","Lila had taken over one end of the table. Her laptop was open, her shoes were tucked beneath her chair, and two boxes of tacos sat beside a pile of snacks.","She pushed one box toward Eira.","\"Dinner survived.\"","\"I thought overtime killed taco night.\"","\"Nothing kills taco night. It just changes the address.\"","Eira sat down and took a bite before opening the briefing packet. She had not realized how hungry she was.","The profiles covered the main investors, Pack leaders, and executives attending the expo. Alpha Sebastian’s appeared several pages in.","Marital status: Married.","Spouse: Not publicly disclosed.","Someone had crossed out the second line and written:","Eira Crawford.","The sharp black handwriting belonged to Alpha Killian.","Below it, another note read:","Personal relationship: Serena Winthrop.","The word Unconfirmed had been written before the entry, then crossed out with one firm stroke.","Eira held out her hand. \"Pen?\"","Lila passed her one.","On the working copy, Eira added a note beside her own name.","Separation pending.","Lila nearly dropped her taco. \"Is that official?\"","\"It will be.\"","\"You’re really leaving him?\" Lila asked.","\"Yes.\"","Her face brightened, then turned serious. \"Do you have somewhere safe to stay?\"","\"I’m with Mrs. Thorne.\"","\"Good. And if that ever gets complicated, I have a furnished apartment two blocks from here. The last tenant moved out, and I haven’t listed it yet.\"","\"Lila—\"","\"I’m not trying to manage your life. I’m offering you a spare key and zero questions.\"","Eira studied her.","They had known each other only a few days. Yet Lila offered help without demanding details, gratitude, or loyalty in return.","\"Thank you,\" Eira said. \"I may not need it, but thank you.\"","\"Great. I’ll cancel the rescue mission.\"","\"You had one?\"","Lila lifted her car keys. \"Getaway car and emergency snacks. The basics.\"","They returned to the packet.","After a moment, Lila asked, \"Did you know about Serena?\"","\"I found out a few days ago. Before that, I trusted him.\"","\"Trusting your husband wasn’t stupid,\" Lila said. \"He was the one who betrayed that trust.\"","The simple answer eased something tight in Eira’s chest.","Lila nodded toward Alpha Killian’s office. \"My brother and I fight about everything, but when I need him, he shows up. Same goes for me.\"","\"You hide it well.\"","\"We’re emotionally constipated. It runs in the family.\"","\"I can hear you,\" Alpha Killian said from his office.","\"Good. Saves me a text.\"","Eira laughed and glanced through the open door.","Alpha Killian had already returned to his report. His sleeves were rolled to his forearms, and the warm desk light traced the hard line of his jaw. One hand rested on the page while the other turned his fountain pen between long fingers.","He looked completely focused.","Completely untouchable.","Then, as if he felt her watching, Alpha Killian lifted his eyes.","Their gazes met through the glass. Alpha Killian’s pen stopped between his fingers.","Something shifted in his silver-gray eyes. Not quite a smile. Not quite a question.","Just enough to send a strange warmth down Eira’s spine.","Eira looked back at the packet, but the words blurred for a moment.","Lila followed her gaze and smiled.","\"Thinking about my brother?\"","\"The report.\"","\"Of course.\""]},{"number":35,"title":"Chapter 35 False Assumptions","paragraphs":["Two hours later, Alpha Killian stepped out of his office, his fountain pen still in hand.","\"That’s enough for tonight.\"","Eira closed her folder. She had already finished the report, but she did not argue.","\"Understood.\"","Lila shut her laptop and reached for her bag.","\"You’re going back to Mrs. Thorne’s, right? I can drive you.\"","Alpha Killian gave his sister a flat look.","\"How many speeding tickets did you get last year?\"","\"That is private information.\"","\"Seven.\"","\"Two of them were unfair.\"","\"I’ll drive her,\" Alpha Killian said.","Lila went still. Her gaze moved from Alpha Killian to Eira, then back to her brother. A slow smile spread across her face.","The silence became awkward.","Eira cleared her throat. \"Thank you, but I can call a ride.\"","\"The car is already downstairs,\" Alpha Killian said. His tone made it clear that the matter was settled.","Lila picked up her bag, still smiling. \"Great. We can all go together.\"","--","A black SUV waited outside Sterling Tower. The driver opened the rear door, and Eira climbed in.","Alpha Killian sat beside her while Lila took the front passenger seat.","Eira had just reached for her seat belt when another car cut into their lane. The driver swerved to avoid it.","The sudden turn threw her sideways.","Alpha Killian caught her around the waist and pulled her against his chest. Her palm landed over his heart, and her lips brushed the edge of his jaw.","They both froze.","His arm remained around her. Beneath her hand, his heart gave one hard beat.","Eira lifted her head, bringing her mouth dangerously close to his. Alpha Killian’s gaze dropped to her lips.","\"Are you hurt?\" he asked, his voice lower than usual.","\"No.\"","For another second, neither of them moved.","Then Alpha Killian released her.","Eira quickly sat up and fastened her seat belt. Heat rushed into her cheeks as she shifted as close to the window as possible.","\"Take it easy,\" Alpha Killian told the driver.","\"My apologies, Alpha.\"","\"It wasn’t his fault,\" Eira said. \"That car cut him off.\"","Alpha Killian glanced at her. \"I know.\"","His tone made it clear that her safety mattered more than who was at fault.","He opened his folder and returned to work.","Eira turned toward the window, keeping as much space between them as she could. Still, she could feel the memory of his hand at her waist and the rough brush of his jaw against her lips.","Fast reflexes. That was all.","After several minutes, the awkward angle made her neck ache. She rubbed the sore spot beneath her ear.","The pages beside her stopped turning.","Alpha Killian looked at the narrow space she had forced herself into, then closed his folder.","\"Pull over.\"","Once the SUV stopped safely at the curb, he got out and opened the front passenger door.","\"Switch with me,\" he told Lila.","Lila looked from her brother to Eira’s flushed face.","\"Why?\"","\"Move.\"","She climbed out slowly, studying her brother as if he had suddenly grown a second head. Alpha Killian waited until she was seated beside Eira before taking the front passenger seat.","The SUV started moving again.","Eira looked at the broad line of Alpha Killian’s shoulders above the seat. He had not asked if she was uncomfortable. He had not explained himself at all.","Maybe he wanted more light to read. Maybe he needed to speak to the driver.","Either reason made sense.","Lila leaned closer. \"He gave up his seat for you.\"","\"He probably wanted more room to work.\"","\"No, he didn’t.\"","\"How would you know?\"","\"Because Killian never sits up front when there’s a driver. He says it makes people think he works security.\"","The SUV stopped outside the Thorne estate twenty minutes later.","Eira stepped out and closed the rear door. Before walking away, she leaned toward the open front window.","\"Thank you for the ride, Alpha Killian.\"","Alpha Killian looked up from the report. For a moment, his eyes held hers.","\"Making sure my staff gets home safely is part of the job.\"","The answer was professional. His gaze was not.","Eira felt that strange warmth again, but dismissed it as simple gratitude.","\"Then you take your job very seriously.\"","\"I take everything seriously, Miss Crawford.\"","\"I’ve noticed.\"","The corner of his mouth moved, almost forming a smile.","\"Good night, Eira.\"","It was the first time he had used her first name.","She paused, though she could not have said why.","\"Good night, Alpha Killian.\"","Something shifted in his eyes, but it disappeared before she could understand it.","Eira straightened and stepped back from the SUV.","The moment the car began moving, Lila leaned between the front seats.","\"Wow. Very professional.\"","Alpha Killian opened the report again. \"What are you talking about?\"","\"The personal ride home. The long look. Calling her Eira.\"","\"Sit back.\"","Lila lowered her voice in a terrible imitation of him. \"’I take everything seriously, Miss Crawford.’\" She pressed a hand to her chest. \"Very smooth. Very subtle.\"","Alpha Killian pressed the button for the privacy screen.","\"Oh, come on,\" Lila said as the divider began to rise. \"You know I’m right.\"","Her laughter followed until the glass sealed off the rear cabin.","Alpha Killian looked into the side mirror.","Eira was still standing beneath the porch light. She watched the SUV leave, one hand resting on the strap of her bag.","Maybe she was only waiting to wave to Lila.","Alpha Killian watched until the car reached the end of the drive and Eira finally turned toward the house.","Then he lowered his eyes to the report.","Three blocks later, he was still on the same page.","--","At eight thirty Saturday morning, Eira met Rachel at a café near the family center.","Rachel wore jeans, a soft sweater, and the nervous smile of someone still worried the offer might be too good to be true.","\"I brought the transfer confirmation,\" Rachel said, sliding her phone across the table. \"The program changed the registration to my name.\"","Eira checked the screen. Everything looked correct.","\"Here are the access badges and course guides.\"","She handed Rachel the welcome packet she had collected from the apartment.","Rachel looked inside, then quickly closed it. \"Are you sure about the price? I can pay more.\"","\"We already agreed.\"","\"But this package is worth thousands.\"","\"Then use what you saved for something the baby will need.\"","Rachel’s eyes softened. \"Thank you.\"","\"Don’t thank me yet. You have two classes today and two tomorrow.\"","They completed the final transfer form together.","Rachel left for the family center, and Eira finished her coffee.","After leaving the café, Eira headed to a salon near the shopping district. Mrs. Thorne had given her a gown for the expo, and Eira wanted to choose a hairstyle that matched it.","She could have gone somewhere quick and cheap.","But the gown had been a thoughtful gift. Treating it like an afterthought felt wrong.","Eira entered Westbridge Galleria and stepped onto the escalator.","As it carried her toward the second floor, movement inside the jewelry boutique below caught her eye.","Serena stood in front of a mirror, a diamond bracelet around her wrist.","Alpha Sebastian was beside her.","He had one hand in his pocket and the other resting lightly against Serena’s back. When she turned toward him, his face softened into the warm smile Eira had once believed belonged only to her.","Eira did not need to hear the conversation.","She had seen enough.","Alpha Sebastian believed his wife was spending the morning learning how to build a family with him.","Meanwhile, he was buying jewelry for the woman he actually wanted.","Before the escalator carried her out of view, Eira took out her phone and snapped one clear photo through the boutique’s open entrance.","Neither Alpha Sebastian nor Serena looked up.","Good.","For years, Alpha Sebastian had expected her to protect his reputation while he did whatever he wanted. She was done keeping his secrets for him.","At the top of the escalator, Eira sent the picture to Susan.","Eira: Please add this to the file."]},{"number":36,"title":"Chapter 36 The Price of Devotion","paragraphs":["Alpha Sebastian spent Saturday trailing Serena through one luxury store after another, his arms loaded with shopping bags.","By seven, she had new dresses, shoes, handbags, and enough jewelry to stock a display case.","At her building, Serena stopped in the lobby and kicked off her heels.","\"I can’t take another step.\"","Alpha Sebastian crouched. \"Hop on.\"","She climbed onto his back, laughing as he carried her into the private elevator and up to the penthouse.","Once inside, he set her on the sofa. Serena kissed the corner of his mouth.","\"Thanks for spoiling me.\"","\"Take a hot shower and get some rest.\"","She glanced at the clock. \"You’re leaving?\"","\"I should get home.\"","If he left now, he could still be back by seven thirty. That was when Eira usually came home, assuming she had returned from the Thorne estate.","Serena caught his wrist.","\"Do you have to?\"","\"Eira and I are still married. Staying here all night would only make things more complicated.\"","Serena stared at him. \"After everything we’ve done, now you’re worried about boundaries?\"","\"Serena.\"","\"Are you falling for her?\"","\"No.\" The answer came fast. \"I loved you then. I love you now.\"","\"Then what is she?\"","\"My wife. I have responsibilities.\"","Serena lowered her eyes. When she looked up, tears filled them.","\"You’re right. This is my fault. I should’ve stopped us that night.\"","\"You did nothing wrong.\"","\"I slept with a married man. If my grandfather finds out, he could pull my research funding. My whole family would turn on me.\"","\"They won’t find out.\"","\"That doesn’t make me feel better.\"","She stepped into his arms and pressed her face to his chest.","\"I never stopped loving you. If I’d come back before your wedding, would you still have married her?\"","\"No.\"","This time, he did not hesitate.","\"We already lost four years.\" Serena looked up at him, a tear sliding down her cheek. \"I can’t lose you again. If all you can give me is stolen time, I’ll take it. I’d rather have part of you than none of you.\"","It was exactly what Alpha Sebastian needed to hear.","He cupped her face. \"You’re the only woman I’ve ever loved.\"","Then he kissed her. His coat stayed by the door.","Serena fell asleep against Alpha Sebastian’s chest.","He reached for his phone and texted Eira.","Sebastian: How was the first workshop?","A few minutes later, she sent him a short summary with a chart of the main points.","Alpha Sebastian smiled. Eira had gone to class. She was taking his offer of a future seriously.","His plan was working.","He had no idea Rachel had sent Eira photos of the class notes. Eira had cleaned them up, added a chart, and forwarded the result.","The more secure Alpha Sebastian felt, the less likely he was to look closely.","He transferred ten thousand dollars to her account.","Sebastian: Stop worrying about work. Focus on becoming a good Luna and preparing for our family. I’ll take care of everything else.","Then he sent another lie.","Sebastian: I had a business dinner that ran late, so I won’t be home tonight. Don’t be upset.","Serena stirred against him.","Alpha Sebastian looked down at the woman he loved, then pictured the wife who had spent four years organizing his life.","In his mind, Serena was love and Eira was duty.","He told himself Eira needed him. She had no Pack or parents to fall back on. Who would take care of her if he let her go?","The thought made him feel noble instead of selfish.","--","Eira saw Alpha Sebastian’s messages over breakfast the next morning.","She nearly choked on her coffee.","A business dinner.","Right.","Apparently, that was what he called spending the night in Serena’s bed.","Before Serena came back, Alpha Sebastian had always made it home after client dinners, no matter how late. If he had too much to drink, he slept in the guest room because Eira hated the smell of alcohol.","The next morning, she would bring him coffee and breakfast. Most days, the smell alone woke him.","For four years, they had shared a home and built a routine. From the outside, they had looked like any other married couple.","As long as no one looked too closely.","Alpha Sebastian had played the devoted husband well.","Maybe that was why the truth had taken her so long to see.","That afternoon, Rachel sent her notes from the second workshop. Eira organized them and forwarded another summary to Alpha Sebastian.","His response came almost at once.","Sebastian: Good. Keep this up.","Eira stared at the message.","Then she muted the conversation.","While Alpha Sebastian congratulated himself on bringing his wife back under control, Eira stood in the sunroom at the Thorne estate with jewelry spread across a long table.","Beatrice fastened a sapphire necklace around Eira’s throat, stepped back, and frowned.","\"No. Too dramatic.\"","She replaced it with an emerald pendant.","\"Beautiful, but not with the gown.\"","Eira stood patiently while Beatrice tried another necklace.","The older woman rarely wore fine jewelry in public. Her simple cardigans and comfortable shoes gave no hint of the collection filling the velvet boxes in front of them.","\"Alaric bought most of these,\" Beatrice said. \"He had terrible taste when we were young.\"","Eira smiled. \"Professor Thorne had strong opinions about everything.\"","\"That’s a polite way to say he was stubborn.\"","Beatrice opened another case.","\"When we first married, he could only afford tiny gold earrings for our anniversary. Years later, after his first major research grant, he came home with sapphires.\"","She held up the necklace and shook her head.","\"He said the blue reminded him of my eyes. My eyes are brown.\"","Eira laughed.","\"That sounds like him.\"","\"He was brilliant in the lab and hopeless everywhere else.\" Beatrice’s face softened. \"Eventually, he learned.\"","She opened a narrow velvet box and removed a strand of pearls.","\"Let’s try these.\"","She fastened the pearls around Eira’s neck and added the matching earrings. Then she turned her toward the mirror.","The pearls gave Eira’s skin a soft glow.","Beatrice nodded. \"That’s the set. Classic, elegant, and perfect with the lace on your gown.\"","Eira studied her reflection. \"I’ll wear them to the expo.\"","\"Of course you will.\" Beatrice began closing the other boxes. \"And you’ll take the rest.\"","Eira turned. \"The rest of what?\"","\"The jewelry.\"","Beatrice pointed at the table as casually as if she were offering leftovers.","\"The emeralds, the sapphires, and the pink diamonds. Take one set in every color. You’ll need options for other events.\"","\"Mrs. Thorne, I can’t accept all of this.\"","\"Sure you can.\"","\"It’s too much.\"","Beatrice settled into a cushioned chair.","\"I’m not giving it to you for free.\"","Eira waited.","\"Alaric and I never had children. I don’t want these pieces locked in a safe for the next fifty years. Jewelry is meant to be worn.\"","She reached for Eira’s hand.","\"So wear it. Take care of it. And when I’m gone, visit us once in a while. Tell Alaric and me what’s happening in your life.\"","Her voice remained light, but her eyes did not.","\"That’s the deal.\"","Eira’s throat tightened.","\"You’re not going anywhere for a long time.\"","Beatrice smiled. \"Then Alaric can keep waiting. Patience was never his strong suit. It’ll be good for him.\"","She pulled Eira down onto the seat beside her.","\"Do you know what he wrote in the letter he left me?\"","Eira shook her head.","Beatrice tightened her fingers around hers.","\"He wrote, ’Beatrice, I’m leaving Eira with you, and I’m leaving you with her. Take care of each other.’\"","Eira’s eyes began to burn."]},{"number":37,"title":"Chapter 37 The Woman in the Mirror","paragraphs":["Beatrice wiped Eira’s tears, her own eyes turning red.","\"Alaric acted tough, but he was a softie underneath. He just hated anyone knowing it.\"","She gently lifted Eira’s chin.","\"I’m telling you this because Sebastian has taken enough from you. One bad marriage doesn’t get to define the rest of your life.\"","Eira nodded.","\"Good. Now cry if you need to, but get some sleep afterward. I refuse to send you to the expo tomorrow with swollen eyes.\"","Beatrice pinched her cheek, then frowned.","\"And eat something. You’re getting too thin.\"","Eira laughed through her tears.","\"That’s better.\" Beatrice squeezed her hand. \"The stylist will be here tomorrow. Hair, makeup, the works.\"","She gave Eira a pointed look.","\"You’re twenty-five, Dr. Crawford. Wear the dress. Put on the heels. Enjoy yourself. You have plenty of time to dress like a retired librarian when you actually become one.\"","\"I’ll try.\"","\"Don’t try. Do it.\"","Eira smiled. \"I will.\"","\"Good. Once the project review is over, you’ll qualify for university housing. And if Stanford has any sense, a faculty position will follow.\"","Beatrice squeezed her hand once more.","\"You’ve spent long enough taking care of everyone else. It’s time you started taking care of yourself.\"","Her voice softened.","\"I’m proud of you.\"","--","The next morning, Eira headed to Sterling Tower in her usual work clothes.","Killian and most of the expo team were already at the venue, leaving the executive floor unusually quiet. Eira spent the morning working with Claire to confirm the guest list, seating chart, and security details.","Just before noon, her phone buzzed.","Martin: The stylist is here.","Eira submitted her half-day request and returned to the Thorne estate.","By the time she entered the guest room, the stylist had covered the vanity with makeup and hair tools.","Eira changed into Beatrice’s lace gown and sat before the mirror.","The stylist swept her hair into a low chignon, leaving a few soft waves around her face. She had just begun Eira’s makeup when Alpha Sebastian called.","\"Are you still at Sterling?\" Alpha Sebastian asked.","\"Why?\"","\"Something came up, so I can’t take you to the expo tonight. Just head home when you’re done.\"","It was not an apology. It was an instruction.","\"That’s fine.\"","\"I knew you’d understand.\"","The call ended before Eira could answer.","Eira set down her phone without asking what had come up. She already knew.","The stylist studied her in the mirror. \"Are those your real lashes?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Lucky you. With those eyes and cheekbones, you’re making my job way too easy.\"","Eira laughed softly. \"I’ll take that as a compliment.\"","\"You should.\"","The stylist finished her makeup and added Beatrice’s pearl necklace and earrings. Then she pointed to a shoe box on the dresser.","\"Those arrived from Sterling.\"","A card rested beneath the designer logo.","For tonight’s event. Size confirmed. Sterling Executive Office.","Inside was a pair of nude heels with thin straps and pearl details at the ankles.","The stylist checked the label and whistled. \"Limited release. Nearly two grand, if you can find them.\"","Eira frowned. \"They’re for work.\"","\"Sure,\" the stylist said, clearly unconvinced. \"Does your boss send every employee sold-out designer shoes in the right size?\"","\"He takes care of his staff.\"","\"If you say so.\"","Eira slipped them on. They fit perfectly.","Once the stylist had finished the last touches, Eira gathered her skirt and headed downstairs.","Twenty minutes later, the Thorne car stopped outside the expo venue. The shoes still looked perfect, though Eira’s feet had already begun to protest.","Martin opened her door and handed her a small embroidered clutch.","Eira stared at it. \"This barely holds my phone.\"","\"It isn’t supposed to hold your entire office.\"","She raised an eyebrow.","Martin smiled. \"Mrs. Thorne’s words, not mine. I’ll be nearby when you’re ready to leave.\"","Eira slipped her phone and cards into the clutch.","\"Thank you.\"","Then she gathered her skirt and stepped out.","--","The expo filled one of the city’s grandest historic hotels. Warm light spilled from its tall windows, and black cars lined the circular drive.","Eira stepped onto the sidewalk and texted Professor Davies and Claire.","Claire called right away.","\"We’re at the main entrance. Where are you?\"","\"About ten feet to your left.\"","Claire turned, scanned the crowd, and looked straight past her.","\"Claire.\"","She turned back and froze.","The lace gown followed Eira’s slim figure without looking too revealing. Beatrice’s pearls glowed against her skin, and the soft waves framing her face made her blue eyes appear even brighter. With her graceful posture and quiet confidence, she looked polished, elegant, and completely out of reach.","Claire’s jaw dropped.","\"No way.\"","Eira raised an eyebrow. \"Is something wrong?\"","\"Wrong?\" Claire hurried over. \"I’ve walked past you twice. I thought you were some actress trying to keep a low profile.\"","Professor Davies joined them and stopped short.","\"Eira?\"","\"Yes, Professor.\"","His surprise softened into a proud smile. \"You look wonderful.\"","\"Thank you.\"","Claire stepped back to take in the gown, pearls, and perfectly styled hair.","\"Okay, this is not just wonderful. You look like old Hollywood walked onto a red carpet and decided to put the rest of us out of business.\"","Eira glanced down at herself. \"That sounds a little dramatic.\"","\"It’s not dramatic if it’s true.\" Claire leaned closer. \"You’re going to break necks in there.\"","\"Let’s try to avoid workplace injuries.\"","Claire laughed. \"There she is.\"","Professor Davies offered Eira his arm.","\"Shall we?\"","Eira accepted it and lifted the hem of her gown as they headed toward the steps.","A bright, excited voice rang out behind them.","\"Wow, Sebastian. This place is unreal. I’ll have enough photos to keep my Instagram feed going for a month.\"","Eira stopped.","Alpha Sebastian answered in the patient tone he usually saved for his younger sister.","\"Slow down, Isabella. We’re waiting for someone.\"","\"I know. Serena said she’d be here in fifteen minutes.\" Isabella laughed. \"Why don’t you take me inside and come back for her? Then the two of you can make your big entrance together. The photographers will go crazy. You’ll look like you belong on the cover of Town & Country.\"","She paused.","\"Way better than you would with... You know what? Never mind.\"","Claire glanced over her shoulder.","\"Isn’t that Sebastian Hale? Everyone on the project thinks he and Dr. Winthrop are together. I figured it was just office gossip.\"","Professor Davies went still.","His gaze moved from Alpha Sebastian to Eira.","Then his expression changed as the pieces fell into place.","\"Eira,\" he said quietly, \"That’s your husband, isn’t it?\"","\"Yes.\"","Professor Davies stared at her.","\"And Dr. Winthrop?\""]},{"number":38,"title":"Chapter 38 The Woman He Never Saw","paragraphs":["Eira tilted her head and answered quietly.","\"His very close old friend. The kind he sleeps with.\"","At that moment, Isabella came up the steps with her arm looped through Alpha Sebastian’s.","Her face lit up at the grand entrance. Beside her, Alpha Sebastian wore his usual polished smile. In his tailored black suit, he looked ready for a photo spread in the society pages.","His gaze started to drift toward Eira.","She turned away.","Professor Davies caught on immediately. He stepped up one stair and shifted in front of her, blocking her from view.","Alpha Sebastian glanced over, but guests crowded the steps. He noticed Professor Davies and Claire, gave them no more than a passing glance, and continued inside with Isabella.","The attendant scanned his invitation.","\"Welcome, Mr. Hale. You’re all set.\"","Alpha Sebastian disappeared through the doors without realizing his wife had been standing only a few feet away.","Claire watched him go, her earlier excitement gone.","Professor Davies lowered his voice. \"So everyone at the institute had it right.\"","\"No. Apparently, adultery is the one commitment he takes seriously.\"","His mouth tightened. \"Do you need a minute?\"","Eira gathered her skirt.","\"For him? I’ve already wasted four years.\"","She lifted her chin and continued up the steps.","--","The hotel’s grand ballroom had been dressed for a red-carpet gala. Chandeliers glittered above the marble floor while investors, researchers, and industry leaders worked the room in tuxedos and evening gowns.","Eira had attended a similar event with Alaric and Beatrice years ago. She had spent the evening hiding behind a column and left as soon as etiquette allowed.","Tonight, she found another quiet corner.","\"I’m going to sit for a minute,\" she told Professor Davies and Claire.","The heels were gorgeous. Her feet had already filed a complaint.","She had barely settled onto a bench when Lila hurried over. \"Eira! I knew it was you.\"","\"From across the room?\"","\"From behind.\"","Alpha Sebastian had walked right past his own wife. Lila had recognized her at once.","\"How?\"","Lila shrugged. \"Different hair, same scent. Plus, you still stand like someone’s about to dump a five-alarm disaster in your lap and call it a tiny favor.\"","Eira moved over. \"Sit.\"","Lila dropped beside her and took one long look.","\"Okay. Damn.\"","\"It’s a dress, Lila.\"","\"No, I’m wearing a dress. You look like you own the hotel and might fire anyone who asks for proof.\"","Eira glanced down at the lace. \"That seems unlikely.\"","\"The gown is perfect, the pearls are classy, and your eyes are doing something unfair in this lighting.\" Lila shook her head. \"You’re all soft and elegant, but you still look like you could destroy a man’s career before dessert.\"","\"That is oddly specific.\"","\"And completely accurate.\"","\"Thank you. I think.\"","Lila kept staring.","\"What?\" Eira asked.","\"I’m adjusting. You usually look ready to pull an all-nighter in a lab. Tonight, you look like the reason half this room forgot what they were saying.\"","Eira laughed.","\"There she is.\" Lila opened her arms. \"Come here. Mandatory friend hug.\"","Before Eira could object, Lila pulled her into a tight hug.","Eira stiffened. She still was not used to affection that came without strings attached.","\"You look amazing,\" Lila declared. \"You smell expensive, and hugging you is doing wonders for my social status.\"","\"Is that the real reason?\"","\"Mostly. The rest is emotional support.\"","Despite herself, Eira relaxed into the hug.","--","Across the ballroom, Alpha Killian noticed his sister practically climbing over someone on a bench.","\"Of course,\" he muttered.","He started toward her.","Then Lila straightened, revealing the woman in her arms.","Alpha Killian stopped.","The lace gown skimmed Eira’s figure and fell in soft folds around her legs. Pearls glowed at her throat, and her low chignon left the graceful line of her neck bare.","But it was not the dress that held his attention.","It was Eira herself.","She was laughing at something Lila had said, her usual reserve briefly gone. Beneath the chandeliers, her blue eyes looked brighter, and the warmth in her face made her seem softer than the quiet, composed woman who worked at his side in Sterling Tower.","Elegant. Composed. Almost untouchable.","\"Is that Ms. Crawford?\" Miles asked beside him.","\"Yes.\"","Alpha Killian answered without looking away.","His body had already shifted in her direction when Miles cleared his throat.","\"Alpha, the potential project partner is waiting. This is our only chance to meet with him tonight.\"","Alpha Killian’s jaw tightened.","He looked at Eira for one second longer.","Then he turned away.","\"Let’s go.\"","--","Serena Winthrop stepped from her car in a wine-red mermaid gown. Rubies flashed at her throat and wrists, and her dark hair fell in polished waves over her bare shoulders.","She had dressed to turn heads.","It worked.","Several guests looked over as she searched the entrance for Alpha Sebastian. When she failed to find him, she sent a text.","His reply came at once.","Sebastian: Meeting an important contact. Go on in. I’ll find you.","So much for making an entrance together.","Serena hid her annoyance and climbed the steps alone.","The attendant scanned her invitation.","\"Dr. Serena Winthrop. Welcome. Your grandfather is one of tonight’s honored guests.\"","\"He’ll be here soon.\"","\"Of course. Enjoy your evening.\"","The Winthrop name opened doors. Within minutes, investors and researchers had gathered around her.","\"How is your grandfather?\"","\"Very well, thank you.\"","\"I heard you recently returned from overseas.\"","\"I did. I’m working on a new research project now.\"","\"What kind?\"","Serena took a glass of champagne from a passing tray.","\"We’re keeping the details under wraps for now.\"","That was enough. The group heard major funding, restricted access, and powerful connections.","Business cards appeared. So did lunch invitations and offers to \"stay in touch.\"","Serena handled them with an easy smile until she spotted Professor Davies and Claire across the ballroom.","\"Excuse me. I see someone I need to speak with.\"","She crossed the room.","Professor Davies noticed her approach and settled into a polite, professional expression.","\"Dr. Winthrop.\"","Claire quickly finished her canapé. \"Hi, Dr. Winthrop.\"","\"Please, call me Serena. Dr. Winthrop makes me sound like my grandfather.\"","Professor Davies did not take the hint.","\"What can we do for you, Dr. Winthrop?\"","Her smile tightened.","\"Is Dr. Crawford here?\"","If Professor Davies and Claire had come, Dr. Crawford was probably nearby.","Serena had spent days trying to meet the researcher who always managed to stay one step ahead of her.","Tonight, she planned to find her."]},{"number":39,"title":"Chapter 39 Who Do You Think?","paragraphs":["\"Dr. Crawford is right over...\" Claire began.","\"She isn’t here,\" Professor Davies cut in.","Claire caught his pointed look and quickly changed course.","\"Right. She skipped tonight. Crowds aren’t really her thing.\"","\"I see,\" Serena said.","A hint of contempt crossed her face. So the brilliant Dr. Crawford could run a lab but not work a room. What a waste of an invitation.","Still, her absence was a relief. Serena had spent weeks trying to meet the researcher who always stayed one step ahead of her, but tonight she had enough to manage.","Her grandfather had refused to show her a photo. She still had no idea that Dr. Eira Crawford and Alpha Sebastian Hale’s quiet wife were the same woman.","Before Serena could leave, Professor Davies spoke.","\"Dr. Winthrop, are you and Sebastian Hale together?\"","Serena paused, then gave him a coy smile.","\"What makes you ask?\"","\"We overheard his sister talking about the two of you.\"","Serena lowered her eyes.","\"We’re keeping it quiet for now. My family doesn’t know, so I’d appreciate your discretion.\"","Professor Davies’s expression hardened.","Claire understood what he was doing and played along.","\"How long have you been together?\"","\"We’ve known each other for almost eight years.\"","\"Did you start dating after you came back to California?\"","\"Not exactly.\" Serena took a sip of champagne. \"We never really lost touch. Sebastian even visited me overseas a few times.\"","Claire kept her tone casual. \"So this didn’t start after you came home?\"","Serena’s smile turned dreamy. \"Some feelings never really go away. We both knew what those visits meant.\"","Professor Davies caught the edge of a nearby cocktail table.","Serena frowned. \"Professor, are you okay?\"","\"I’m fine. Just a little light-headed.\" He forced a tired smile. \"You two go enjoy the party.\"","Before Serena could ask another question, someone called her name from across the ballroom.","She spotted Ethan Yates, one of Alpha Sebastian’s closest friends.","\"I should go say hello. Excuse me.\"","As soon as she walked away, Professor Davies lowered himself into a nearby chair.","Claire followed him. \"You’re not fine.\"","\"She just admitted this started long before she came home, while Sebastian was still married to Eira.\" His face tightened. \"Give me a minute.\"","Claire’s expression darkened. She searched the ballroom for Eira, but Professor Davies caught her arm.","\"Don’t bring her over here, and don’t tell Serena who Dr. Crawford is.\"","\"Why not?\"","\"Because Eira deserves one night without becoming the hottest piece of gossip in the entire industry.\"","\"You think Serena will make a scene?\"","\"I think she’ll do whatever it takes to hold on to Sebastian.\"","Claire glanced toward Serena, then nodded.","\"Fair enough.\"","\"If you see Eira, act normal. Just don’t do anything that leads Serena to her.\"","\"Got it.\"","--","A few minutes later, Claire passed Eira near the edge of the ballroom.","Serena was still standing with Ethan across the room, and Claire could feel her watching. Remembering Professor Davies’s warning, she kept moving.","\"Claire?\"","Claire’s shoulders tightened. She glanced back with an apologetic grimace, then reached for her phone.","Eira’s phone buzzed inside her clutch.","Claire: Long story. Professor’s orders. Serena is looking for Dr. Crawford, and she still doesn’t know that’s you. We’re trying to keep it that way.","Eira read the message twice.","Eira: Understood.","\"Who was that?\" Lila asked, appearing with two champagne flutes.","\"My friend Claire.\"","\"Why is your friend texting you from twenty feet away?\"","\"Apparently, we’re being discreet.\"","Lila handed her a glass.","\"I don’t drink,\" Eira said.","\"It’s a prop. Hold it and everyone assumes you’re busy.\"","\"Doing what?\"","\"Looking expensive and emotionally unavailable.\"","Eira accepted the glass. \"You’ve put a lot of thought into this.\"","\"I grew up at parties like this. Ninety percent of networking is holding a drink and pretending you remember someone’s name.\"","\"Shouldn’t you be working the room?\"","\"I could, but then you’d be sitting here alone, looking like a very elegant hostage.\"","\"I’m fine.\"","\"Sure. And I love making small talk with venture capitalists.\"","Lila nodded toward the crowd.","\"Come on. One lap. If anyone corners us, I’ll fake an emergency.\"","\"What kind?\"","\"Food poisoning is a classic. Family crisis if we need something with range.\"","Eira sighed and stood. \"One lap.\"","\"Look at you, living on the edge.\"","They moved through the ballroom together. Lila sampled hors d’oeuvres from passing trays and handed the best ones to Eira.","\"This one has goat cheese.\"","\"No.\"","\"You haven’t tried it.\"","\"I can smell it.\"","\"More for me.\"","Their easy conversation drew a few curious looks.","Eira ignored them.","Serena did not. She noticed Lila first. Then her gaze shifted to the woman beside her.","Her smile vanished.","That face.","Ethan followed her stare. \"Do you know her?\"","Serena did not answer.","The woman looked familiar, but the possibility made no sense. Eira wore plain clothes, kept her head down, and stayed away from events like this. She certainly did not walk through galas wearing pearls and a designer gown as if she belonged at the center of the room.","And Alpha Sebastian had claimed he was meeting someone important.","Unease tightened Serena’s chest.","\"Look at that woman.\"","Ethan glanced over. \"What about her?\"","\"Doesn’t she look familiar?\"","He studied Eira. \"Not to me.\"","\"It’s Eira.\"","Ethan looked again. \"Wait. Sebastian’s wife?\"","Serena’s jaw tightened. \"Yes.\"","Before Ethan could say more, Serena was already crossing the ballroom.","He exchanged a look with his date, then followed Serena with the woman at his side.","Serena moved quickly, though she tried not to look as if she were rushing.","\"Eira?\"","Eira turned.","Serena stopped short.","So did Ethan and his date.","Up close, there was no mistaking her. But this was not the quiet woman Alpha Sebastian had kept in the background for four years.","Eira wore a pale, figure-skimming gown with a modest neckline and a clean, elegant silhouette. It accentuated her slender frame without making her look as though she had tried too hard. Her golden hair framed her face, and her makeup was soft enough to highlight rather than conceal—the vivid blue of her eyes, the delicate curve of her lips, and the refined lines of her features.","She wasn’t dressed to impress anyone. She didn’t need to be. There was something quietly captivating about her—a kind of beauty that felt natural, unforced, and impossible to overlook. Attention found her wherever she stood.","Ethan stared openly.","His date glanced from Eira to Serena, then quietly adjusted her expression as if she had just realized the evening had become far more interesting.","Even Lila looked pleased by their reaction.","For one sharp second, Serena felt overdressed. Her red gown and rubies, chosen to command the room, suddenly seemed loud beside Eira’s effortless elegance.","She recovered first.","\"What are you doing here?\"","Eira glanced at the champagne flute in her hand, then back at Serena.","\"Attending the expo. Most people figured that out from the invitation.\"","Ethan coughed into his fist, hiding a laugh.","Color rose in Serena’s cheeks.","\"You know what I mean. Who brought you?\"","The question came out too fast and far too sharp.","Eira heard the fear beneath it.","Serena was not worried about how she had gotten inside. She was worried Alpha Sebastian had brought her.","Eira let the silence stretch before lifting one eyebrow.","\"Who do you think?\" The color drained from Serena’s face.","Ethan fell silent.","So Alpha Sebastian had brought his wife after all.","It made sense. Whatever Alpha Sebastian claimed to feel for Serena, Eira was still his legal wife—and his Luna. Bringing her to an industry gala was hardly unusual.","What was unusual was Alpha Sebastian letting anyone see her.","For four years, he had kept Eira out of the public eye. Why bring her into the spotlight now?","Was he finally planning to acknowledge their marriage?"]},{"number":40,"title":"Chapter 40 The Wife He Underestimated","paragraphs":["Serena’s expression darkened, but too many people were watching for her to lose her cool.","\"So Sebastian brought you after all.\"","Eira let her believe it.","Serena’s gaze dropped to the pearls. \"A little safe for tonight, don’t you think? I’m surprised Sebastian didn’t pick something with more impact.\"","Lila gave a short laugh.","\"Those are perfectly matched South Sea pearls. It’s called quiet luxury. Not everything has to scream across the room for attention.\"","Her gaze flicked briefly over Serena’s red gown and rubies.","The insult landed. Ethan looked down, hiding a smile, while his date suddenly became very interested in her champagne.","Serena’s eyes narrowed. \"I don’t remember asking you.\"","\"No, but you were embarrassing yourself in public. I figured I’d help.\"","Ethan’s date nudged him when his attention returned to Eira.","\"Stop staring,\" she muttered.","\"She’s Sebastian’s wife,\" he said. \"I’m allowed to be surprised.\"","Serena’s smile tightened at the word wife.","She turned on Lila. \"Be careful. Eira has a lot more experience playing these games than you do.\"","Lila smiled. \"Was that advice? Cute.\"","Eira glanced at Serena. \"She does have seniority.\"","Lila caught on immediately.","\"Good point. We should always listen to our elders.\"","A woman standing nearby covered a laugh with her glass. Serena heard it. Heat climbed into her cheeks.","Eira and Lila turned to leave, but Serena stepped closer.","\"Don’t look so pleased with yourself. Four years of marriage, and this is the first time Alpha Sebastian has taken you anywhere.\"","Eira met her glare.","\"And after all these years, he still introduces you as a friend.\" Her gaze moved briefly over Serena’s face. \"Sounds like neither of us won much.\"","Serena’s expression hardened.","\"He may not touch you, but he can’t keep his hands off me.\"","Eira remained unmoved.","\"You slept with a married man. That’s not the flex you think it is.\"","Ethan coughed into his fist, but this time it did nothing to hide his laugh. Even his date’s lips twitched.","Serena glanced around. Several guests were openly watching now, though none were close enough to hear every word.","\"You really don’t care?\" she whispered.","\"About keeping him?\" Eira linked her arm through Lila’s. \"No.\"","She took one step, then paused.","\"You wanted him, Serena. You can have him.\"","Serena’s fingers tightened around her clutch.","Eira’s eyes dropped to them before returning to her face.","\"But if you’d really won, you wouldn’t be this scared of me showing up.\"","Serena went still.","That was the part she could not deny.","Eira walked away with Lila on her arm. Behind them, the conversation around Serena slowly resumed, but the curious glances did not stop.","Lila held herself together until they were safely out of earshot.","\"Okay,\" Lila said. \"That was beautiful. No notes.\"","\"You were the one insulting her jewelry.\"","\"I corrected her jewelry knowledge. Totally different.\"","Eira gave her a look.","Lila lifted the champagne flute in her hand.","\"Give me five minutes and this glass. I can turn their affair into the hottest story in the room.\"","\"Do you want to hijack the gala your brother spent months organizing?\"","Lila considered it.","\"How attached is he to the current program?\"","\"Lila.\"","\"Fine.\" She sighed. \"No public scandal.\"","\"Then leave it alone.\"","--","The moment Eira and Lila were out of earshot, Ethan pulled out his phone.","Ethan: Seb, your Luna and Serena just went a few rounds.","Alpha Sebastian had just stepped out of a private meeting room. He stared at the message.","He had not brought Eira to the expo.","How could the two women have crossed paths?","Sebastian: Eira is there?","Ethan: Kind of hard to miss her.","Sebastian: Who brought her?","Ethan: No idea. She’s been with Lila Sterling all night.","Alpha Sebastian frowned.","Ethan: And your wife is actually working the room. Didn’t know she had it in her.","His frown deepened.","Sebastian: Stay out of it.","Ethan: Gladly. You’ve got enough problems without borrowing mine.","Alpha Sebastian pocketed his phone.","Lila Sterling had been with Eira all evening.","His first thought was Alpha Killian.","--","Alpha Killian emerged from the meeting room just as Alpha Sebastian pocketed his phone.","\"Impressive,\" Alpha Killian said. \"You actually got Dr. Shaw to vouch for you.\"","Alpha Sebastian gave him a tight smile.","\"Some of us have to build our own connections. Others are born with an entire Pack’s contact list.\"","Alpha Killian’s expression stayed cool. \"Careful, Hale. Taking shots at my family won’t make yours any more impressive.\"","\"At least I don’t bring another Alpha’s wife to a gala.\"","That told Alpha Killian everything he needed to know.","Eira had not come with Alpha Sebastian.","But she had entered with a black-and-gold invitation, not a standard project pass. Alpha Killian had not sent it, and Dr. Thorne—the only other obvious connection with that level of access—wasn’t attending tonight.","So who had put her on the VIP list?","Interesting.","Alpha Sebastian clearly knew even less about his wife than Alpha Killian had thought.","A faint smile touched Alpha Killian’s mouth.","\"You showed up planning to escort another woman, but you’re worried about who brought your wife?\"","\"That’s not what I said.\"","\"You didn’t have to.\"","Alpha Killian walked past him.","Miles fell into step beside him. \"Sir, I just spoke with Miss Sterling.\"","\"And?\"","\"She took Dr. Crawford to meet your parents.\"","Alpha Killian stopped.","\"Of course she did.\"","He changed direction and headed straight for the ballroom.","By the time Alpha Killian found them, his mother was already talking to Eira.","\"Lila tells me you’re Alpha Killian’s executive assistant.\"","\"Yes, Luna Sterling.\"","Eira stood straight, every word polite and careful.","Luna Seraphina smiled. \"Please, call me Seraphina. ’Luna Sterling’ makes this sound like a Pack council hearing.\"","A small smile touched Eira’s lips. \"All right.\"","Luna Seraphina opened her mouth to ask another question.","\"Mom.\"","Alpha Killian stepped between them before the conversation turned into a full background check."]},{"number":41,"title":"Chapter 41 The Line He Crossed","paragraphs":["Luna Seraphina glanced back at her son and sighed.","At twenty-eight, Alpha Killian could stare down an entire boardroom without blinking. Put him in front of a woman he actually liked, and suddenly he had the timing of a teenager.","\"Must you make one word sound like a Pack emergency?\" she asked.","Alpha Killian gave her a flat look. \"I said Mom.\"","\"And somehow made it sound like a threat.\"","Luna Seraphina turned back to Eira.","\"Come by the house with Lila sometime. I promise good food and only a reasonable amount of family chaos.\"","The invitation caught Eira off guard. She had not expected such easy warmth from Lila’s mother, much less the Luna of the Reed Pack.","\"I’d like that. Thank you, Seraphina.\"","\"Good.\" Luna Seraphina patted her hand. \"Lila, help me find your father.\"","\"But I just—\"","Lila looked at Alpha Killian, then at Eira. She caught on almost at once.","\"Oh. Right. Dad. Very urgent.\"","She flashed Eira a grin.","\"Killian, take care of my friend.\"","\"Lila.\"","She was already walking away with their mother.","Eira watched them disappear into the crowd. The cold, untouchable CEO of Sterling Group was apparently the least powerful person in his own family.","\"Alpha Killian.\"","\"Mm.\"","Alpha Killian turned to her and forgot what he had meant to say.","The soft makeup brought out the clear blue of her eyes. Pearls rested at the base of her throat, drawing his attention to the bare line of her neck.","His gaze lingered.","Eira glanced down at her gown. \"Is there a problem?\"","He cleared his throat. \"Who did you come with tonight?\"","\"Sebastian Hale.\"","A quiet laugh escaped him. \"Didn’t you say you were leaving him?\"","Eira’s shoulders stiffened. \"I said I was handling it.\"","\"That wasn’t my question.\"","\"And my marriage isn’t your business.\" She turned toward the buffet. \"I’m going to get something to eat.\"","\"Eira.\" Alpha Killian lightly caught her forearm.","She looked down at his hand, then back at him. \"I’m not your assistant tonight.\"","He released her at once.","\"No,\" he said. \"So what is this—one last night of playing Mrs. Hale?\"","His gaze shifted toward Serena.","\"But Hale came here expecting to spend the night with another woman\"","Before Eira could answer, a smooth voice cut between them.","\"Why is Alpha Sterling so interested in someone else’s marriage?\"","Alpha Sebastian stepped up beside Eira.","Without asking, he slid an arm around her waist.","Eira went rigid.","Then she caught his wrist and pulled his hand away.","\"Don’t touch me.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression tightened, but he kept his smile in place for the guests passing nearby.","Alpha Killian’s gaze dropped to Alpha Sebastian’s hand, then rose slowly to his face.","\"Alpha Hale.\"","\"Alpha Sterling.\"","The names sounded less like greetings and more like warnings.","Alpha Sebastian turned to Eira. \"We need to talk.\"","\"No. You need to explain why you told me to go home while you waited here for Serena.\"","A couple passing nearby slowed.","Alpha Sebastian lowered his voice. \"Not here.\"","\"Then you shouldn’t have started this here.\" Eira turned away.","Alpha Sebastian caught her wrist.","\"Let go.\"","His grip tightened.","\"If you’ll excuse us,\" he said to Alpha Killian.","\"We’re not going anywhere,\" Eira snapped.","Alpha Sebastian ignored her and pulled her toward the edge of the ballroom.","She dug in her heels, but the thin straps slid against the marble.","\"Sebastian, stop.\"","He kept moving, his polished smile never slipping. To anyone watching from a distance, he looked like a husband guiding his wife through the crowd.","Up close, his fingers were digging into her wrist.","Eira twisted hard, trying to break his grip.","\"Take your hand off me.\"","One heel slipped free. She stumbled, and Alpha Sebastian barely slowed.","Her second shoe caught against the floor. Eira kicked it off rather than risk breaking an ankle and planted her bare feet on the marble.","Alpha Killian was already moving.","He picked up the first heel as he passed, then caught the second by its ankle strap without breaking stride. A thin smear of blood marked the leather where it had rubbed Eira’s skin raw.","His expression turned glacial.","Then he followed.","--","Alpha Sebastian dragged Eira into a quiet hallway off the ballroom. The music faded as the doors closed behind them.","The moment they were alone, Eira tore her wrist free.","\"What the hell is wrong with you?\"","Alpha Sebastian turned on her.","For the first time that night, he truly looked at his wife.","The lace gown followed the clean lines of her body. Her makeup was soft, and her dark hair was pinned in an elegant style. Even barefoot, she looked calm and confident.","She no longer looked like the wife who had spent four years waiting for him at home.","She looked like a woman who had already moved on.","The thought hit harder than he expected.","\"Why are you dressed like this?\"","Eira stared at him. \"It’s a black-tie gala. What did you expect, sweatpants?\"","\"Don’t play dumb.\"","\"I’m not the one asking why someone wore an evening gown to a formal event.\"","His jaw tightened.","\"You came with Killian Sterling.\"","\"No, I didn’t.\"","\"Then why have you been with his sister all night?\"","\"Lila is my friend. I don’t need your permission to have one.\"","Alpha Sebastian barely heard her. All he could see was the dress, the makeup, and the way Alpha Killian had stared at her.","Jealousy burned through him.","He reached up and pulled the jeweled pins from her hair.","One caught in the strands and tugged hard at her scalp. Eira flinched as her hair fell over her shoulders.","\"What are you doing?\"","\"You don’t look like yourself.\"","\"I look exactly like myself. You just never bothered to notice.\"","His face hardened.","He dragged his thumb across her mouth, smearing her lipstick.","\"Who are you trying to impress?\"","Eira slapped his hand away.","\"Don’t touch my face.\"","Alpha Sebastian grabbed her upper arm.","\"You dressed up for Sterling, didn’t you? Is this your way of getting into his bed?\"","Eira shoved him with both hands.","He stumbled back half a step, more shocked than hurt.","\"Not everyone is like you,\" she snapped. \"Stop putting your guilt on me because you hate what you see in the mirror.\"","Alpha Sebastian froze. \"What do you know?\"","\"Enough.\"","She turned away, but he caught her again.","\"Tell me.\"","\"Let go.\"","Eira twisted free. Her bare foot slipped on the polished floor, but a hand caught her before she fell.","Alpha Killian steadied her, then stepped between them. Her heels hung from one hand, a thin streak of blood staining one strap.","His silver eyes fixed on Alpha Sebastian.","\"Back off, Hale.\"","\"This is between me and my wife.\"","\"She told you to stop. That makes it everyone’s business.\"","Alpha Sebastian stepped forward. \"Stay out of my marriage.\"","Alpha Killian did not move.","\"Touch her again, and security walks you out. After that, she can press charges.\""]},{"number":42,"title":"Chapter 42 The Choice He Made","paragraphs":["Alpha Killian looked down at Eira. \"Are you hurt?\"","Eira glanced at her scraped wrist and bleeding heel. \"I’ve been better.\"","Alpha Sebastian reached for her again.","Eira stepped back before he could touch her. \"I already warned you.\"","At the same moment, Alpha Killian shifted between them.","\"Try it,\" he said. \"Let’s see how far you get.\"","Alpha Sebastian stopped. \"She’s my wife, Alpha Sterling.\"","Alpha Killian looked at Eira’s bare, dirty feet and the blood running down her heel.","\"Then why are you hauling her around like checked baggage?\"","Alpha Sebastian finally noticed the blood.","\"Where are your shoes?\"","Alpha Killian raised the heels in one hand. \"They came off while you were dragging her across the ballroom.\"","Alpha Sebastian ignored him.","\"I’ll have someone bring you flats,\" he told Eira. \"Next time, don’t wear heels if you can’t walk in them.\"","\"The heels weren’t the problem. You were.\"","His face hardened. \"Do you have to turn everything into a fight?\"","\"You grabbed me after I told you to stop. That’s not a fight. That’s you refusing to take no for an answer.\"","Approval flickered in Alpha Killian’s eyes.","Alpha Sebastian caught it.","\"Is this because Alpha Sterling is here? You finally found an audience, so now you’re putting on a show?\"","\"Leave him out of this.\"","\"Then why did you come with him?\"","Alpha Killian answered before Eira could.","\"What’s wrong with an executive assistant attending a business event with her boss?\"","Eira glanced at him. He had not actually brought her, but he clearly had no intention of correcting Alpha Sebastian.","Alpha Sebastian opened his mouth, but Alpha Killian looked past him.","\"There’s your date. Maybe you should explain why you left her waiting while you manhandled your wife.\"","Serena stood at the end of the hallway, her eyes shining with tears.","Alpha Sebastian followed Alpha Killian’s gaze.","\"She’s not my date. Serena is a friend.\"","Eira gave a humorless smile. \"Of course she is.\"","Serena flinched.","Alpha Sebastian turned back to Eira. \"You know there’s nothing going on between us.\"","\"I know what you tell people.\"","Her voice carried clearly down the hallway.","Serena’s face went pale. She lowered her eyes and walked away.","\"Serena.\"","Alpha Sebastian took a step after her, then stopped.","He looked between the two women.","Eira stood barefoot with blood on her heel, bruises forming around her wrist, and lipstick smeared across her mouth.","Serena was leaving in tears.","For one moment, the choice could not have been clearer.","His phone buzzed.","I’m going home. Sorry I got in the way.","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened.","\"Eira, wait here.\"","She stared at him. \"Excuse me?\"","\"I need to make sure Serena’s okay. We’ll finish this conversation later.\"","\"There’s nothing left to finish.\"","Alpha Sebastian ignored that and lowered his voice.","\"What did you mean earlier when you said not everyone was like me?\"","\"You heard me wrong.\"","\"No, I didn’t.\"","\"You were angry. You heard what you wanted to hear.\"","He studied her face, but Eira gave him nothing.","She glanced toward the ballroom.","\"You should go. Your friend is upset.\"","Alpha Sebastian searched her expression for jealousy.","There was none.","That bothered him more than anger would have.","\"We’ll talk at home.\"","Then he went after Serena.","Eira watched him disappear.","He had seen the blood on her heel and the marks on her wrist. He had still chosen Serena.","It hurt less than it should have.","Maybe because, by now, it was exactly what she expected.","A pair of white ballet flats landed softly in front of her.","Eira looked up.","Alpha Killian stood beside her, his expression unreadable. Miles waited a few steps behind him with a small first-aid pouch.","\"You keep emergency shoes at a black-tie gala?\" Eira asked.","\"Miles does.\"","Miles gave her a polite nod. \"The event team plans for wardrobe problems.\"","Alpha Killian took the pouch from him.","\"That’ll be all.\"","Miles left without comment.","Eira reached for the flats.","Alpha Killian moved them out of reach.","\"Sit down first.\"","\"I can handle a blister.\"","\"Clearly.\"","She gave him a cool look. \"You’re very helpful when you’re being insulting.\"","\"I have a wide range of skills.\"","Despite herself, Eira almost smiled.","A bench stood against the hallway wall. She sat and reached for the first-aid pouch, but Alpha Killian opened it before she could. \"I can do it myself.\"","\"I know.\"","\"Then give me the bandage.\"","\"No.\"","Eira raised an eyebrow. \"Are all Alphas this controlling?\"","\"Only when someone is about to put a sock over an open blister.\"","She looked down at her heel.","He had a point.","That made him more annoying.","--","Serena waited in the foyer between the ballroom and the terrace until she saw Alpha Sebastian coming.","Then she turned away.","\"Serena.\"","He caught up with her near the doors.","She wiped quickly beneath one eye.","\"You should go back. If Eira sees us together, she’ll get the wrong idea.\"","\"She’s still in the hallway.\"","Again, it was the wrong answer.","Serena wanted him to say that Eira did not matter. She wanted him to choose her without hesitation.","Instead, he had left her waiting all evening, then followed his wife out of the ballroom.","\"If you wanted to spend tonight with Eira, you could have told me,\" she said. \"I would’ve brought someone else.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression changed.","\"You’re not bringing another man.\"","\"Why not?\"","\"Because I don’t want you to.\"","\"That isn’t an answer.\"","His jaw tightened.","\"Fine. I’d be jealous.\"","Serena lowered her eyes to hide her satisfaction.","\"Now you know how I felt watching you with your wife.\"","\"She didn’t come with me.\"","Serena looked up.","\"What?\"","\"She came with Killian Sterling.\"","It was the explanation Alpha Sebastian had already chosen to believe, despite what both Eira and Alpha Killian had told him.","Serena’s eyes widened. \"Alpha Sterling brought her?\"","\"They’re not together.\" His answer came too fast.","Serena heard the fear beneath it.","So did Alpha Sebastian.","Alpha Killian Sterling had noticed Eira.","The Alpha of the Sterling Pack could have almost any woman he wanted. Why would he choose a Wolfless Omega with no powerful family or social connections?","Serena forced herself to breathe.","It had to be temporary. Curiosity, perhaps. Men like Alpha Killian sometimes became interested in women who were different from their usual circle.","That did not mean he would claim her. It certainly did not mean the Reed Pack would welcome her.","The thought calmed Serena.","She slipped her fingers through Alpha Sebastian’s.","\"Come outside with me. I need some air.\"","He let her lead him onto the terrace.","Most guests had remained inside because of the evening chill. The far end of the terrace lay in shadow, screened from the ballroom by tall potted trees.","Serena stopped there.","\"Serena, what are we doing?\"","She stepped into his arms.","\"Something we should have done a long time ago.\"","She kissed his neck, then his jaw.","When her mouth found his, Alpha Sebastian caught her waist.","For a moment, he kissed her back.","Neither of them noticed the figure standing behind the glass doors at the far end of the terrace.","A phone rose quietly.","The red recording light came on."]},{"number":43,"title":"Chapter 43 May I Have This Dance?","paragraphs":["Kate stared at the blurry video on her phone with the guilty expression of someone who had just stumbled onto the scandal of the year.","Miles walked over. \"What did you do?\"","She quickly locked the screen. \"Why do you always assume I did something?\"","\"Because you look like you just got caught red-handed.\"","Kate glanced around, then pulled him closer.","\"I caught Alpha Hale and Dr. Winthrop making out on the terrace.\"","Miles stared at her. \"You’re kidding.\"","She played the video.","The footage was shaky, but Alpha Sebastian and Serena were easy to recognize. The audio was even clearer.","Miles lowered his voice. \"Please tell me you didn’t stand there filming the whole thing.\"","\"Would you rather I’d walked over and asked them to smile for the camera?\"","Natalie joined them. \"What’s going on?\"","Kate showed her the clip.","Natalie’s face turned cold. \"So much for Serena being ’just a friend.’\"","\"I’m sending this to Eira,\" Kate said.","\"Not tonight,\" Miles replied. \"She’s already been through enough.\"","Kate frowned. \"Then what do we do with it?\"","\"Send me a copy. It happened at a Sterling event, so Alpha Sterling needs to know. You can give Eira the original after the gala.\"","Kate sent him the file.","Miles checked that it had arrived and headed for the private meeting rooms.","He had barely made it down the hall when he ran into Luna Seraphina and Lila.","\"Luna Sterling. Ms. Sterling.\"","\"Hello, Miles.\" Luna Seraphina’s smile was pleasant, but her next question was anything but casual. \"How is Eira settling in as Killian’s assistant?\"","Miles immediately understood what she was really asking.","\"She’s quiet, but she’s extremely sharp. She caught a serious mistake in the technical section of a proposal before it reached a potential partner. She saved the team from a very expensive embarrassment.\"","Luna Seraphina looked impressed.","\"Quiet and capable,\" she said. \"A little like Killian.\"","Lila laughed. \"Not when they’re together. Eira actually argues with him.\"","Miles nodded. \"She also tells him no, which is still a new experience for him.\"","Luna Seraphina’s eyebrows rose.","\"And how does Killian take that?\"","\"Better than anyone expected.\"","Lila grinned. \"He talks way more when she’s around.\"","\"That’s true,\" Miles said. \"Most people run out of things to say when Alpha Sterling gives them that look. Ms. Crawford just gives it right back.\"","Luna Seraphina’s smile slowly widened. \"How interesting.\"","Miles suddenly felt as if he had said too much.","\"Has she ever made him lose his temper?\" Luna Seraphina asked.","\"Not exactly.\"","\"Too bad.\"","Miles blinked.","Luna Seraphina gave him an innocent smile. \"If she ever gets under his skin, let me know. I’ve been trying to get a real reaction out of that boy for years.\"","\"Of course, Luna.\"","\"Tell me too,\" Lila added. \"I want details.\"","Miles looked between them.","He excused himself before either woman could ask more questions.","--","Miles found Alpha Killian talking with Professor Davies outside one of the private meeting rooms. Claire stood beside the professor.","Miles approached. \"Alpha, I have something you need to see. It concerns Eira Crawford.\"","Claire went still.","Alpha Killian caught the reaction at once.","\"You know her?\"","Professor Davies rested a hand on Claire’s shoulder. \"Eira studied under Alaric. We’ve crossed paths.\"","It was a smooth answer, but not a complete one.","Alpha Killian looked between them.","They clearly knew more than they were willing to say. He filed that away for later.","\"Send it,\" he told Miles.","A moment later, the video appeared on his phone.","The footage was shaky, but Alpha Sebastian and Serena were impossible to miss. The audio was crystal clear.","Alpha Killian watched them kiss on the terrace. His expression turned cold.","\"Save a copy with event security,\" he said. \"Restricted access.\"","\"Got it.\"","\"And make sure Kate gets a bonus.\"","Miles raised an eyebrow. \"For filming two guests hooking up?\"","\"For documenting misconduct at a Sterling event.\"","Miles took the hint. \"Right.\"","Alpha Killian glanced toward the ballroom.","Alpha Sebastian had dragged Eira across the floor, left her bleeding in a hallway, and then gone straight to Serena.","Now he was back at the party as if nothing had happened.","\"Move the sponsor remarks up.\"","\"Now?\"","\"Now.\"","Minutes later, Alpha Killian stepped onto the stage.","He thanked the sponsors and research teams, then kept the rest short.","Before leaving the microphone, he looked across the ballroom.","\"We’d also like to recognize one of tonight’s industry partners, Sebastian Hale, CEO of Hale Group Technologies.\"","Miles gave the lighting crew a quick signal.","A spotlight landed on Alpha Sebastian.","Serena happened to be standing at his side, close enough that her shoulder brushed his arm.","A murmur spread through the room. Together under the spotlight, they looked less like friends and more like a couple making their first public appearance.","Serena smiled as if the attention belonged to her.","Alpha Sebastian did not.","After what had happened on the terrace, the sudden attention put him on edge. When Alpha Killian’s gaze held his for one cold second, Alpha Sebastian wondered if the spotlight was more warning than welcome.","As Alpha Killian left the stage, the orchestra began a waltz.","Serena held out her hand to Alpha Sebastian.","\"Dance with me.\"","He hesitated and searched the ballroom again.","He was looking for Eira.","Serena knew he was worried his wife might see them together. She did not care.","Few people at the gala knew Alpha Sebastian was married. Even fewer knew Eira was his wife. Tonight, Serena had stood beside him under the spotlight. If they danced together now, the city’s Pack leaders and business elite would draw their own conclusions.","By morning, the rumor mill would have them halfway to the altar.","The more people saw Serena as his future Luna, the harder it would be for Alpha Sebastian to deny what they were.","\"Come on,\" she said. \"Everyone’s watching.\"","Alpha Sebastian finally took her hand.","Serena led him onto the dance floor. He placed one hand on her waist, but his gaze continued to move around the room.","\"You’re distracted,\" she said.","\"I’m not.\"","\"You’re looking for Eira.\"","His jaw tightened. \"I’m making sure she doesn’t start something.\"","Serena smiled. \"Sure.\"","They both knew Eira had not been the one making a scene tonight.","When Alpha Sebastian failed to find her, he slowly relaxed. His hold became less stiff, and Serena moved closer.","To the people watching, they looked less like old friends and more like a couple making their relationship public.","--","Eira stood near the far wall, outside the brightest part of the ballroom.","Alpha Sebastian and Serena could not see her.","She could see them perfectly.","They moved together with practiced ease. Serena smiled up at him, and Alpha Sebastian looked more comfortable than he had all night.","What a classy pair. A cheating husband and his so-called friend, dancing in public like they deserved applause.","\"Eira.\"","Lila stepped beside her and followed her gaze.","Her expression darkened.","\"You have got to be kidding me.\"","Eira took a sip of water. \"Apparently, subtlety isn’t their strong suit.\"","Lila looked toward the stage.","\"Fine. If they want to put on a show, we’ll give the room something better to watch.\"","She spotted Alpha Killian and raised her hand.","\"Killian!\"","Eira caught her arm. \"Lila, don’t.\"","\"Too late.\"","Alpha Killian looked over. Lila pointed toward the dance floor, then nodded at Eira.","His gaze moved from his sister to Alpha Sebastian and Serena. His expression cooled as he understood what Lila wanted.","A few seconds later, he joined them.","Then Alpha Killian held out his hand.","\"Miss Crawford,\" he said, his silver eyes fixed on hers. \"May I have this dance?\""]},{"number":44,"title":"Chapter 44 Who’s Playing Whom?","paragraphs":["Eira placed her hand in Alpha Killian’s.","\"You may.\"","Across the ballroom, Alpha Sebastian went still.","A moment earlier, he had been smiling at Serena. Now he was staring at Eira as if she had just set fire to his entire life.","He started toward her.","\"Ow!\"","Serena stumbled and grabbed his arm.","\"I think I twisted my ankle.\"","Alpha Sebastian stopped at once. He helped her to a nearby chair and crouched to check her ankle.","Eira watched him fuss over Serena’s ankle.","Minutes earlier, he had dragged his own wife across a marble floor, left her bleeding in a hallway, and blamed her shoes.","The bar was not low. It was six feet underground.","A dry laugh escaped her.","Then Alpha Killian’s fingers closed around hers, and his other hand settled lightly at her waist.","\"Is your heel going to be a problem?\" he asked.","\"It’s a blister, not a broken leg.\"","\"That wasn’t a yes.\"","Eira looked up at him. \"I’ll survive.\"","His hold remained careful. He did not pull her closer or assume she needed help. He simply waited for her to follow his lead.","Apparently, basic respect could feel impressive when someone had gone without it for long enough.","The music carried them into the waltz.","Eira matched Alpha Killian’s steps with ease. After the first turn, his eyebrows rose.","\"You know how to dance.\"","\"You sound shocked.\"","\"I keep finding out you can do things no one bothered to mention.\"","\"You’ve known me for less than a month.\"","\"And yet the list keeps growing.\"","Alpha Killian guided her through another turn.","\"Who taught you?\"","\"Professor Thorne. He refused to let me embarrass him at an awards dinner.\"","\"A doctor, a researcher, and a trained dancer.\"","\"He believed in being prepared.\"","Alpha Killian leaned slightly closer. \"For everything?\"","Eira met his eyes. \"Everything except you, apparently.\"","A low laugh escaped him.","Several nearby guests glanced over. Alpha Sterling rarely laughed in public, especially while dancing with a woman most of them did not recognize.","The whispers began almost at once.","Who is she?","Isn’t that his assistant?","Since when does Killian Sterling dance?","Eira heard them but kept moving.","For once, she did not care what anyone thought.","--","Alpha Sebastian straightened after checking Serena’s ankle, but his attention had already moved elsewhere.","Eira was dancing with Alpha Killian.","She moved with quiet confidence, her hand resting on Alpha Killian’s shoulder as he guided her across the floor. She looked calm. Comfortable.","She looked like she belonged with him.","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened.","For four years, Eira had been part of the background of his life. She handled his home, managed his Pack, and waited for him without complaint.","Now she was in the center of the ballroom, and another man was seeing everything Alpha Sebastian had ignored.","Serena followed his gaze.","\"Sebastian? What are you staring at?\"","\"I’m watching the dance floor.\"","\"No. You’re watching your wife.\"","His expression hardened, but he did not deny it.","The music slowed.","Alpha Killian raised their joined hands, and Eira turned beneath his arm. Her dress moved softly around her legs as she returned to him.","For one brief second, they stood closer than before.","Their eyes met.","The crowd faded into the background. Eira became aware of the warmth of his hand at her waist and the steady way he held her gaze.","Something shifted inside her chest.","She stepped back before she could examine it.","The final note faded.","Alpha Killian bowed. Eira answered with a graceful dip of her head.","Applause rose from the guests nearest the dance floor, then spread through the room.","Alpha Killian straightened but did not release her hand.","Eira glanced down at their joined fingers.","\"Planning to keep that?\"","\"I was considering it.\"","\"That sounds expensive.\"","\"I can afford it.\"","She pulled her hand free, but the corner of her mouth lifted.","Across the room, Alpha Sebastian stood frozen.","Everyone around him was talking about the woman Alpha Sterling had chosen to dance with.","Who was she?","How long had they known each other?","Was she really only his assistant?","The attention Alpha Sebastian and Serena had enjoyed only minutes earlier had shifted completely to Eira and Alpha Killian.","Serena watched Alpha Sebastian’s rigid expression and felt her stomach drop.","This was not simple anger.","He was jealous.","--","Eira had barely sat down beside Lila when Alpha Sebastian walked over.","She looked past him toward Serena.","\"Shouldn’t you be checking on your friend? That ankle looked serious.\"","Alpha Killian paused with his wineglass near his mouth. Lila hid a smile.","Alpha Sebastian ignored the jab.","\"Why did you dance with Sterling?\"","Eira raised an eyebrow. \"Because he asked.\"","\"That’s it?\"","\"Most invitations work that way.\"","His jaw tightened. \"You knew everyone was watching.\"","\"So did you when you danced with Serena.\"","\"That was different.\"","\"Of course it was.\" Eira lifted her water glass. \"The rules always change when they apply to you.\"","Alpha Sebastian reached for her hand. \"We need to talk.\"","She pulled away.","\"No.\"","His face hardened. \"Don’t make a scene.\"","\"You came to my table. The scene is yours.\"","\"This is between me and my wife.\"","Alpha Killian set down his glass.","\"Then you picked a strange place to discuss it.\"","Alpha Sebastian forced a tight smile. \"Alpha Sterling, stay out of my marriage.\"","Eira answered before Alpha Killian could.","\"He doesn’t need to. I already told you no.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s phone buzzed. Serena’s name appeared on the screen.","Eira glanced at it.","\"Your friend is waiting.\"","\"I’ll explain everything later.\"","\"Save it. I didn’t ask.\"","\"We’ll talk at home.\"","\"You keep saying that like you still get a vote.\"","Across the ballroom, Serena sat with one hand resting on her supposedly injured ankle.","\"Sebastian,\" she called.","Alpha Sebastian looked between them, then turned and walked away.","Lila watched him go. \"Wow. He really does come running every time she calls.\"","Eira took a sip of water. \"Some patterns never change.\"","Alpha Killian leaned closer, one hand resting on the back of her chair.","\"Miss Crawford.\"","She looked up.","His silver eyes held hers.","\"Now that he’s gone, answer one question.\"","\"What?\"","\"Did you dance with me because you wanted to?\"","His gaze flicked toward Alpha Sebastian.","\"Or were you just using me to get under his skin?\""]},{"number":45,"title":"Chapter 45 Whose Girlfriend?","paragraphs":["Eira tilted her head and held Alpha Killian’s gaze.","\"What makes you think you weren’t using me too, Alpha Sterling?\"","His expression did not change, but his eyes sharpened.","\"Hale Group and Sterling Group have been at each other’s throats for years,\" she continued. \"You knew exactly what dancing with Sebastian Hale’s wife in front of half the city would do to him.\"","\"You’re giving me too much credit. My sister called me over.\"","\"And you didn’t waste the opportunity.\"","Alpha Killian leaned closer. \"Neither did you.\"","Eira looked away.","\"Maybe we both got what we wanted.\"","\"And what did you want?\"","She glanced toward the dance floor, where Alpha Sebastian had disappeared into the crowd.","\"To prove I was done standing in the shadows.\"","Alpha Killian studied her face.","Eira gave a small shrug. \"If you expected Sebastian to care, you misread him.\"","Alpha Killian’s mouth curved slightly.","\"You really believe that?\"","\"I lived with him for four years. I know exactly how little I matter to him.\"","Alpha Killian said nothing.","Alpha Sebastian’s reaction had told a very different story.","--","Alpha Sebastian returned to Serena’s chair and found it empty.","A server directed him to a side hall, where Serena sat beside Isabella with a tissue in her hand.","Isabella glared at him. \"Nice going. You made her cry.\"","\"It’s just my ankle,\" Serena said softly.","\"Give me a break. I saw what happened.\" Isabella turned on Alpha Sebastian. \"You spent the whole dance staring at Eira. And where did she get that dress? People are saying it’s vintage couture. Those pearls probably cost more than my car.\"","\"I didn’t buy them.\"","Isabella paused. \"Then who did?\"","Alpha Killian Sterling came to mind, and Alpha Sebastian’s wolf stirred.","\"That’s none of your business.\"","\"Fine. But why are you defending her? Serena has been waiting for you all night, and you barely noticed.\"","\"Eira is my wife,\" Alpha Sebastian snapped. \"She’s our pack’s Luna. She is family.\"","The words left his mouth before he could stop them.","The hallway fell silent.","Serena’s eyes filled with tears.","\"I understand,\" she said with a weak smile. \"I’m the outsider.\"","\"Serena, that’s not what I meant.\"","\"It’s fine.\"","She stood and limped away.","Isabella shoved Alpha Sebastian’s arm. \"Go after her.\"","\"Stay out of this.\"","\"She came back because she loves you. Are you really going to let her walk away?\"","Alpha Sebastian hesitated.","Only for a second, but it bothered him.","He had always loved Serena. At least, that was what he had believed.","So why was he thinking about Eira in Alpha Killian’s arms?","\"Sebastian!\" Isabella snapped.","He cursed under his breath and followed Serena.","He caught up with her near the lobby.","\"Serena, wait.\"","She kept moving.","\"You shouldn’t be walking on that ankle.\"","\"I said I’m fine.\"","Alpha Sebastian stepped in front of her and glanced down. There was barely any swelling.","Before he could question it, Serena looked up at him.","\"Do you remember what you promised me when we were younger?\"","His expression tightened.","\"You said you would always love me,\" she continued. \"You said we would have a family. You said you would make sure I never had to beg investors for the freedom to do my work.\"","\"I remember.\"","\"Then why did you defend Eira?\" Her voice broke. \"You called her family. What does that make me?\"","Alpha Sebastian had no answer.","Years ago, he had built his future around Serena. He had worked endless hours, chased investors, and pushed Hale Group to the top because he wanted to give her everything.","Then she had left.","By the time she came back, he was married.","Serena saw the doubt in his eyes and changed course at once.","\"I’m sorry,\" she said. \"I shouldn’t have pushed.\"","She wrapped her arms around him.","\"I know this is complicated. I don’t want to make it harder.\"","Alpha Sebastian remained still.","\"I love you,\" she whispered. \"That hasn’t changed.\"","Serena could not lose him now. His love was only part of it. Without him, she would also lose the money, influence, and protection of the Hale name.","After a long pause, Alpha Sebastian placed a hand on her back.","\"I love you too.\"","The answer came out of habit.","For the first time, it sounded more like a line he had memorized than the truth.","--","Once Serena had calmed down and fixed her makeup, she and Alpha Sebastian returned to the ballroom.","Alpha Sebastian immediately searched the crowd for Eira.","She was nowhere in sight.","Instead, he spotted Isabella holding court with several young Pack heirs near the bar. Felix Shaw stood among them.","Alpha Sebastian walked over.","\"Mr. Shaw.\"","Felix turned with a smile. \"Alpha Hale. Good to see you again. Our grandfathers go way back, so just call me Felix.\"","He offered his hand, and Alpha Sebastian shook it.","Felix glanced at Serena. \"And you are?\"","Before Alpha Sebastian could answer, Isabella linked her arm through Serena’s.","\"This is Serena Winthrop, my brother’s girlfriend. She just got back from overseas, and she’s consulting on a federally funded defense project.\"","A brief, awkward silence followed.","Alpha Sebastian’s expression tightened at the word girlfriend, but Serena smiled as if the introduction were perfectly natural.","\"It’s nice to meet you.\"","\"You too,\" Felix said politely, though his eyes flicked toward Alpha Sebastian.","\"My grandfather is Dr. Victor Winthrop,\" Serena added. \"I believe he and your grandfather are old friends.\"","Recognition crossed Felix’s face.","\"Of course. Dr. Winthrop’s granddaughter. I’ve heard a lot about your family.\"","Isabella beamed. \"Serena and Sebastian have known each other forever. Honestly, I’m just waiting for them to make it official so Serena can finally be part of the family for real.\"","She had never considered Eira worthy of the title.","\"Isabella,\" Serena said with a shy laugh. \"Don’t put him on the spot.\"","The color in her cheeks suggested she did not mind at all.","Alpha Sebastian shot his sister a warning look.","Isabella only rolled her eyes.","Felix turned back to Serena. \"If you’re working in defense research, maybe you can help me with something. Do you know Dr. Crawford?\"","Serena paused, then lifted her chin slightly.","\"We’re attached to the same research program. Our teams overlap.\"","Felix’s face lit up.","\"Seriously? My grandfather said Dr. Crawford might be here tonight. I came hoping to meet her.\"","\"I haven’t seen her,\" Serena replied. \"She probably skipped the gala. From what I’ve heard, she avoids public events.\"","Felix tried to hide his disappointment.","\"That’s too bad. I’ve got about a dozen questions about her papers.\"","A familiar voice sounded nearby.","\"Only a dozen?\"","Everyone turned.","Lila Sterling was walking toward them with Eira beside her.","Isabella’s face twisted.","\"Look who’s back,\" she muttered. \"Sterling’s glorified assistant.\"","She had meant to speak under her breath.","She failed.","The nearby conversations went quiet.","Alpha Sebastian looked at her sharply. \"Isabella.\"","\"What?\" Isabella said. \"She’s been following the Sterlings around all night like she belongs here.\"","Eira met her gaze.","\"I was invited. You’re the one insulting people right in front of your hosts.\"","A few guests looked away to hide their smiles.","Isabella’s face flushed.","Felix barely noticed the exchange. He was staring at Eira.","First came confusion.","Then recognition hit him. His eyes widened.","\"Dr. Crawford?\""]},{"number":46,"title":"Chapter 46 Mistaken Identity","paragraphs":["Felix Shaw had seen Eira once before in a photograph in his grandfather’s study.","The picture showed a room full of leading researchers, most of them over fifty. Only three younger faces stood out, and only one was a woman.","Felix remembered her.","His grandfather had mentioned Dr. Crawford many times. Still, the photograph was several years old, and he had never met her in person.","He stared at Eira.","\"Dr. Crawford?\"","Several guests turned toward them.","Eira’s pulse jumped.","She had told Lila and Alpha Killian only two days ago that she had only a master’s degree. Admitting the truth now would raise questions she was not ready to answer.","Felix stepped closer and offered his hand.","\"I’m Felix Shaw. My grandfather talks about you all the time.\"","Eira recognized the last name at once. Felix was the grandson of one of the senior researchers she respected most.","She gave him a polite nod but did not take his hand.","\"I’m afraid you have the wrong person, Mr. Shaw.\"","Felix lowered his hand, clearly confused.","Isabella gave a sharp laugh.","\"Of course he does. Eira isn’t a doctor. She’s Alpha Killian Sterling’s executive assistant.\"","Her gaze moved over Eira’s dress.","\"She usually looks nothing like this. I guess the right dress can fool anybody.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s face darkened.","\"Isabella, enough.\"","\"What? It’s true.\"","Lila stepped forward.","\"At least Eira has a job. Your entire résumé is spending your brother’s money and running your mouth.\"","Isabella’s face turned red.","\"You don’t know anything about me.\"","\"I know enough.\"","Isabella opened her mouth, but one look at Lila’s expression made her think twice.","Felix barely noticed their argument. He continued studying Eira’s face.","\"The picture in my grandfather’s study is old, but you look exactly like her.\"","\"Pictures can be misleading,\" Eira said calmly.","\"Have you ever met Dr. Crawford?\" Serena asked.","Felix shook his head. \"No. I’ve only seen that photograph.\"","Serena relaxed.","\"Then it’s an honest mistake. Dr. Crawford keeps a low profile, and there aren’t many recent photos of her online.\"","\"Exactly,\" Alpha Sebastian said. \"Eira isn’t the researcher you’re looking for.\"","Felix looked at him.","\"You sound pretty sure. Do you two know each other?\"","The question brought an awkward silence.","Eira looked at Alpha Sebastian.","So did Lila.","Only minutes earlier, Isabella had introduced Serena as Alpha Sebastian’s girlfriend. If Alpha Sebastian admitted Eira was his wife, he would also have to explain why he had arrived with another woman.","Felix’s grandfather held several patents Hale Group had been trying to license. If Felix left tonight thinking Alpha Sebastian was a liar and a cheat, any chance of working with the Shaw family could disappear.","Alpha Sebastian told himself Eira would understand.","They had kept their marriage private for four years. One more lie should not matter.","But when he looked at her, the words caught in his throat.","Felix frowned. \"Well?\"","Alpha Sebastian finally answered.","\"We’re friends.\"","Lila stared at him. \"Seriously?\"","Serena smiled and slipped her hand into Alpha Sebastian’s.","Eira looked at their joined hands, then turned back to Felix.","\"He’s right. We’re just friends.\"","Her voice was steady.","Something inside Alpha Sebastian sank.","Felix frowned. \"That took both of you a while to answer.\"","Eira gave him a small smile. \"Some friendships are complicated.\"","\"Eira,\" Alpha Sebastian said.","She ignored him.","\"Come on, Lila. I’m ready to go.\"","\"Same.\"","Lila linked arms with her and headed for the exit.","Alpha Sebastian reached for Eira as she passed, but she stepped out of range without even looking at him.","Serena tightened her grip on his hand.","\"Sebastian, let her go.\"","He pulled free. \"I need to talk to her.\"","Then he went after his wife.","Behind him, Serena’s smile disappeared.","---","Outside the hotel, Eira rested her hand on the passenger door of Lila’s bright red Ferrari.","\"Eira!\"","Alpha Sebastian hurried down the steps after her.","For one brief moment, Eira remembered another night years ago. Alpha Sebastian had run across a street to reach her, breathless and smiling.","That was the night she had accepted his proposal.","The memory faded as quickly as it came.","Lila stepped between them. \"What do you want, Alpha Hale?\"","Alpha Sebastian barely looked at her. His attention stayed on Eira.","\"I need to explain what happened with Felix.\"","\"You called me your friend,\" Eira said. \"There isn’t much to explain.\"","\"Dr. Shaw owns a patent Hale Group has been trying to license for months. What Felix tells him could make or break the deal.\"","\"So you lied to protect your business.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened. \"I was trying to avoid a scene. Bella had just introduced Serena as my girlfriend. If I told Felix you were my wife, I would’ve had to explain the whole mess in front of everyone.\"","Eira almost laughed.","\"That sounds like a problem you created all by yourself.\"","\"I didn’t have time to fix it.\"","\"You had time to tell the truth.\"","Alpha Sebastian fell silent.","Then he tried a different approach.","\"You know how important the Shaw deal is. I told you about it.\"","\"I remember.\"","She remembered better than he did.","Months earlier, Alpha Sebastian had complained that Dr. Shaw refused to take his calls. Eira had quietly mentioned Hale Group during one of her own conversations with the researcher.","That was the only reason Alpha Sebastian had ever gotten a meeting.","He still had no idea.","Alpha Sebastian studied her calm face. \"So you understand why I did it?\"","\"I understand exactly why you did it.\"","Relief crossed his face too quickly.","\"You’re not mad?\"","\"It’s fine.\"","The relief disappeared.","She had not forgiven him. She simply no longer cared enough to argue.","\"Eira, what does that mean?\"","\"It means Felix’s opinion, the patent, and whatever story you tell about Serena are no longer my problem.\"","She pulled open the car door.","\"Go back inside. Your girlfriend is waiting.\"","\"She isn’t my girlfriend.\"","\"You should probably clear that up with your sister. She seems confused.\"","\"Eira.\"","She paused and looked at him.","Alpha Sebastian had followed her outside expecting anger. Anger would have meant he could still explain himself. He could apologize, argue, or somehow pull her back into the same old fight.","Instead, she looked tired.","Worse, she looked done.","\"I’ll fix this,\" he said.","\"You don’t need to fix it for me.\"","Eira got into the car.","Lila gave Alpha Sebastian a cold smile. \"For a guy chasing a major patent, you’re not very good at protecting valuable things.\"","She slid behind the wheel and drove away.","Alpha Sebastian remained outside the hotel, watching the red taillights disappear.","A few blocks later, Lila glanced at Eira.","\"Why did you tell him it was fine?\"","\"Because it doesn’t matter anymore.\"","\"That man denied you were his wife in front of a room full of people.\"","\"And soon, I won’t be.\"","Lila glanced over. \"Wait. Alpha Sebastian already signed?\"","\"We both signed the settlement agreement. The lawyers are handling the rest.\"","A pleased smile spread across Lila’s face. \"Good. It’s about time.\"","Eira looked out the window. \"It’s easier than staying.\"","Lila reached across the console and briefly squeezed her hand.","\"Then you made the right call.\"","\"Thank you.\"","Lila turned her attention back to the road, but her thoughts were already racing.","Sebastian Hale was finally on his way out.","That did not mean Eira belonged to Alpha Killian. Eira was not anyone’s prize to claim.","Still, for the first time, Lila thought her stubborn brother might actually have a chance.","If he was smart enough not to blow it."]},{"number":47,"title":"Chapter 47 Proper Medicine","paragraphs":["Alpha Sebastian returned to the reception, distracted and distant. Serena called his name twice before he noticed her.","Some guests were having a good night.","Alpha Sebastian was not.","Alpha Killian certainly was.","He had just received a message from his sister saying Eira had finally signed the divorce papers. The process was officially underway.","Alpha Killian replied: [You’re just finding this out?]","The smugness in that single line was unmistakable.","Lila nearly threw her phone. Instead, she hooked her arm through Eira’s.","\"We’re the best pair in the world, aren’t we?\"","Eira had no idea why Lila looked so puffed up, but she could not resist the charm.","\"Of course.\"","\"And I’m way better than my brother, right?\"","Eira did not hesitate. \"Absolutely.\"","Lila grinned and typed out a response dripping with satisfaction. She got no reply.","He was probably fuming.","\"Eira, are you in a hurry to get home?\" Lila blinked at her.","\"Why?\"","\"We should celebrate! Celebrate you ditching that loser!\"","Eira paused. The wind stung her cheeks. Then she nodded.","\"You’re right. We should.\"","\"Then leave it to me. I know the perfect place.\"","Lila drove them to a low-lit tavern tucked into a quiet street. Live music drifted from inside. The atmosphere was warm, intimate, never overwhelming.","She pulled Eira upstairs to a private corner table with the best view in the house.","\"I’ll let you in on a secret,\" Lila said with a wink. \"I own this place.\"","Eira raised an eyebrow. \"Really?\"","A server brought them a pitcher of the house sangria and two glasses.","\"I invested in the place a couple of years ago,\" Lila explained. \"Professor Chase practically lives in the lab, which means I do too. I needed somewhere that had nothing to do with research.\"","She filled both glasses.","\"Try this. It’s our signature sangria.\"","Eira took a sip. It was sweet, tart, and dangerously smooth.","\"That barely tastes like alcohol.\"","\"Exactly.\"","They raised their glasses.","\"To freedom,\" Lila said. \"And to never settling for someone who treats you like a backup plan.\"","Eira touched her glass to Lila’s.","\"To freedom.\"","\"And if you never want another relationship, that works too.\"","\"How generous of you.\"","\"I’m supportive like that.\"","Eira smiled and took another sip.","She rarely drank, and she had never spent an evening like this with a friend. No work. No responsibilities. No one waiting at home to criticize her.","For once, she could simply relax.","The first pitcher disappeared faster than either of them expected.","When the server brought another, Lila waved away Eira’s concern.","\"It’s mostly fruit.\"","It was not mostly fruit. By the time Eira noticed the room spinning, Lila had already lowered her head to the table.","\"Lila?\"","No answer.","Eira leaned closer. Lila snored. \"So much for being prepared.\"","Eira tried to stand, but the floor shifted under her feet. She quickly dropped back into the booth.","Neither of them could drive.","She picked up her phone and called Lila’s brother.","Alpha Killian answered before the second ring.","\"Eira?\" His voice came through so clearly that she pulled the phone away from her ear.","\"Why are you so loud?\"","There was a brief pause. \"Have you been drinking?\"","Eira looked at the empty bottle. \"Maybe.\"","\"Where’s Lila?\" Eira glanced across the table.","\"Sleeping.\"","Alpha Killian went silent for one dangerous second. \"Where are you?\"","\"At her bar.\"","\"Which bar?\"","\"The one she owns.\"","\"That does not narrow it down.\"","Eira frowned. \"How many bars does she own?\"","\"Apparently one more than she told me about.\"","He took a slow breath. \"Send me your location.\"","Eira tapped the screen several times. \"I think I did.\"","\"You sent me a taco emoji.\"","\"Oh.\"","\"Hand the phone to an employee.\"","A server passed by, and Eira stopped him. He gave Alpha Killian the address, then returned the phone.","\"I have it,\" Alpha Killian said. \"Stay upstairs. Don’t drink anything else.\"","Alpha Killian grabbed his keys and left the gala. Fifteen minutes later, he pulled up outside the bar.","Alpha Killian found the women in the upstairs booth.","Lila was asleep on the table.","Eira was still awake, though barely. She rested her head in one hand and reached for the bottle with the other.","Alpha Killian took it away. \"That’s enough.\"","Eira slowly raised her head. Her cheeks were flushed, and her blue eyes struggled to focus.","Then Alpha Killian noticed the redness around them and the dried tear tracks on her cheeks.","Whatever lecture he had planned died on his tongue.","\"Come on,\" he said. \"We’re leaving.\"","\"Where are we going?\"","\"Home.\"","He reached for her hand, but Eira pulled away. \"I don’t have one.\"","Her voice cracked.","Fresh tears rolled down her cheeks.","Alpha Killian sat beside her and took a napkin from the table. He gently turned her face toward him and wiped away the tears.","Eira stared at him through unfocused eyes. \"Mom?\"","Alpha Killian froze.","\"Mom,\" she whispered again.","Before he could correct her, her face crumpled. \"Sebastian brought another woman into our bed.\"","Alpha Killian’s hand went still.","\"He never loved me. He married me to make Serena jealous.\" The words came faster now. \"Four years of my life, and I was just part of some stupid game.\"","\"You weren’t.\"","\"He won’t even let me go. He wants his wife at home cooking and cleaning while he plays boyfriend with her.\"","She wiped her face with the back of her hand.","\"But I’m done. He can keep the whole damn marriage.\"","Her voice dropped to a broken whisper.","\"Mom, can I come home for the holidays? You won’t send me away again, right?\"","Alpha Killian’s chest tightened.","\"No,\" he said quietly. \"I won’t send you away.\"","\"And can you make that spicy chicken?\" Her lips trembled. \"The kind that makes my eyes water?\"","\"Sure.\"","\"I miss it.\"","The tears started again.","Alpha Killian had no idea how to comfort her. He only knew he could not leave her sitting there crying.","He slipped one arm behind her back and the other beneath her knees.","Eira did not resist as he lifted her.","\"Mom,\" she murmured against his chest. \"I need a Band-Aid.\"","\"Where?\"","She pressed one hand over her heart. \"Here.\"","Alpha Killian looked down at her.","\"Okay,\" he said. \"I’ll get you one.\"","He carried her downstairs and settled her in the back seat beside Miles.","Then he returned for Lila.","Unlike Eira, his sister went over his shoulder like a sack of potatoes.","Lila stirred. \"Worst brother ever.\"","\"You’re welcome.\"","Once Lila was safely in the car, Alpha Killian stopped at the convenience store next door.","He returned a few minutes later with a box of Band-Aids."]},{"number":48,"title":"Chapter 48 Uninvited","paragraphs":["When the gala finally wound down, Serena left the ballroom on Alpha Sebastian’s arm, smiling as she said good night to investors, researchers, and Pack leaders.","As far as she was concerned, the evening had gone perfectly.","She had been introduced as Dr. Victor Winthrop’s granddaughter and a consultant on a federally funded defense research initiative. More importantly, Isabella had introduced her as Alpha Sebastian’s girlfriend, and no one had corrected her.","Not right away, at least.","Alpha Sebastian Hale had become one of the most closely watched young Alphas in the business world. With Serena beside him, they looked like the kind of power couple society pages loved.","The local grapevine would do the rest.","Several guests stopped them on the way out. Some asked Serena about her research. Others congratulated Alpha Sebastian on Hale Group’s recent growth.","Serena enjoyed every second of it.","Once the crowd began to thin, Isabella joined them with a satisfied smile.","\"See? Serena fits into your world. Unlike Eira, who barely knows how to act at an event like this.\"","Alpha Sebastian shot her a cold look.","\"Drop it, Isabella.\"","She rolled her eyes.","She still could not understand why he kept defending Eira. Yes, Eira had cleaned up well tonight. Yes, Killian Sterling had asked her to dance.","So what?","An Alpha like Killian did not fall for women like Eira. If he was interested, it was probably temporary.","Then another thought struck Isabella.","If something was going on between Eira and Killian, Alpha Sebastian could use it. At the very least, it would keep Eira from playing the innocent victim when the divorce became public.","Alpha Sebastian noticed the look on her face.","\"Whatever you’re planning, don’t.\"","\"I’m not planning anything.\"","\"That look says otherwise.\"","Isabella folded her arms. \"Why are you always taking her side? Did you forget she slapped me?\"","\"You had it coming.\"","Her mouth fell open. \"Seriously?\"","Serena touched Alpha Sebastian’s arm.","\"Take it easy. Bella’s only looking out for you.\"","\"Exactly,\" Isabella said, moving closer to Serena. \"At least someone appreciates me.\"","Alpha Sebastian looked unimpressed.","Before Isabella could continue, she spotted Felix Shaw heading toward the main entrance with an older man.","Professor Davies and Claire walked behind them. Miles and two members of the Sterling event team followed close by.","Miles stepped forward to open the door.","\"Dr. Shaw, Alpha Sterling had to leave unexpectedly. He asked me to see you out.\"","Dr. Shaw waved off the apology.","\"No need. I’ve been finding my own way out of buildings for seventy years.\"","Felix smiled. \"He’s not kidding. He refuses help on principle.\"","\"I refuse unnecessary fuss,\" Dr. Shaw corrected.","He walked with a steady stride and carried himself with the quiet authority of a man who had no reason to impress anyone.","Isabella recognized Felix but not his grandfather.","She gave him a bright smile. \"Felix, calling it a night?\"","\"Yes, Ms. Hale.\"","His response was polite but distant.","Alpha Sebastian and Serena approached.","\"Dr. Shaw,\" Alpha Sebastian said. \"It’s good to see you again.\"","Serena offered a professional smile. \"Good evening.\"","Dr. Shaw nodded to Alpha Sebastian, then turned to her.","\"I don’t believe we’ve met.\"","\"I’m Serena Winthrop.\"","Felix added, \"Dr. Victor Winthrop’s granddaughter.\"","Recognition crossed Dr. Shaw’s face, but it did not make him friendlier.","\"I see.\"","Professor Davies glanced at Serena’s hand resting on Alpha Sebastian’s arm. His expression cooled.","Claire noticed but kept her eyes forward.","Isabella jumped into the silence.","\"This is my brother, and Serena is his girlfriend.\"","Dr. Shaw turned his cool gaze on her.","\"I asked Ms. Winthrop.\"","Color rushed into Isabella’s face. Felix gave her an apologetic look, but she quickly stepped back.","Alpha Sebastian had planned to introduce Serena as his date for the evening. But Miles and several Sterling employees were standing nearby. Anything he said could get back to Eira.","So he chose the safest answer. \"Serena and I are old friends.\"","Serena’s smile stiffened.","Miles raised an eyebrow. \"That’s interesting. Ms. Hale introduced Ms. Winthrop as your girlfriend, and that version of the story has already made its way through half the gala.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression cooled. \"My sister got carried away.\"","\"Then you may want to clear that up,\" Miles said pleasantly. \"The local grapevine is already working overtime.\"","Dr. Shaw studied Alpha Sebastian.","\"Then Eira Craw...\"","Professor Davies cut in before he could finish.","\"Dr. Shaw, it’s late. We can pick this up another time.\"","Dr. Shaw caught the warning and nodded.","\"Fair enough. Felix, let’s go.\"","Alpha Sebastian and Serena stepped aside as the group headed outside. Miles waited until Dr. Shaw and Felix were in the car before closing the door.","As soon as they pulled away, Felix looked at his grandfather.","\"You really don’t like the Winthrops.\"","\"I don’t trust Victor Winthrop.\"","\"Why?\"","Dr. Shaw looked out the window.","\"He’s a capable researcher, but his lab runs on connections. His relatives get positions they haven’t earned, and junior researchers do the work while senior names take the credit.\"","Felix frowned. \"You think Serena is part of that?\"","\"I think she’s had every door opened for her. I haven’t seen enough of her work to know whether she belongs in the room.\"","\"She’s consulting on a federal defense project.\"","\"A fancy title on a guest list proves nothing.\"","Felix thought about that for a moment.","\"That’s why you respect Dr. Crawford. Her work speaks for itself.\"","\"Exactly.\"","Felix hesitated. \"That really was Dr. Crawford tonight, wasn’t it?\"","Dr. Shaw gave him a pointed look. \"You knew it was.\"","\"I suspected it. She denied it.\"","\"Then take the hint.\"","Felix winced.","\"So why is she hiding who she is?\"","\"That’s her business. Claire worked on her research team, and Professor Davies is clearly protecting her privacy. You should do the same.\"","Dr. Shaw’s voice hardened.","\"No calls. No posts. Don’t even mention it to your friends.\"","\"I won’t.\"","After a moment, Felix asked, \"What about the patent Hale Group wants?\"","\"They’re not getting it.\"","Felix looked at him in surprise.","Dr. Shaw’s expression cooled.","\"Eira was the reason I agreed to meet Alpha Sebastian in the first place. Tonight, he denied she was his wife because telling the truth might hurt his image.\"","\"So he lied to protect the deal.\"","\"And lost it anyway,\" Dr. Shaw said. \"I don’t trust valuable research to a man who changes his story whenever honesty becomes inconvenient.\"","Felix glanced back at the hotel.","Alpha Sebastian had spent the evening trying to protect his reputation.","Instead, he had cost himself the deal he wanted most.","--","Alpha Sebastian had the driver drop Isabella off first, then take Serena home.","When they reached her building, he stayed in the car.","\"Good night.\"","Serena stared at him. \"You’re not coming up?\"","Alpha Sebastian did not answer. He told the driver to leave and pulled out his phone.","Serena stood at the curb as the car disappeared down the street. She stamped her supposedly injured foot, no longer bothering to limp.","She knew exactly where he was going.","Alpha Sebastian called Eira twice on the way to the Thorne house. Both calls went unanswered.","By the time he reached the suburbs, it was well past midnight.","Martin opened the door in a robe, surprise crossing his face.","\"Alpha Hale? What are you doing here this late?\"","Alpha Sebastian glanced past him into the house.","\"Could you tell Eira I’m here? She isn’t answering her phone.\""]},{"number":49,"title":"Chapter 49 The Thorne Estate Door","paragraphs":["Martin’s expression remained calm.","\"Mrs. Thorne and Ms. Crawford have both turned in for the night. Mrs. Thorne has trouble sleeping, so I’m afraid I can’t wake the house at this hour.\"","The lie came easily. Martin had spent too many years managing the Thorne household to let an angry Alpha read anything on his face.","Alpha Sebastian studied him but found nothing.","\"So Eira is here.\"","Martin offered a polite smile. \"As I said, it’s late.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s unease deepened. Eira’s flat voice outside the hotel still echoed in his head.","It’s fine.","She had not sounded angry. She had sounded done.","\"Do you have a guest room?\" he asked. \"I’ll wait until morning.\"","\"I’m afraid that won’t be possible.\"","\"I’m her husband.\"","Martin’s smile did not move.","\"Since Dr. Alaric Thorne passed away, the family no longer hosts overnight guests.\"","The message was clear. Husband or not, Alpha Sebastian was not welcome.","His jaw tightened.","\"Tell Eira I came by.\"","\"I’ll let her know.\"","\"And tell her to come home.\"","Martin’s expression cooled slightly.","\"I’ll tell her you stopped by. What she does after that is up to her.\"","Before Alpha Sebastian could argue, Martin wished him good night and closed the door.","Alpha Sebastian stood on the porch for several seconds before returning to the car.","By the time he reached home, it was after midnight.","He went upstairs to change and stopped in front of the open closet.","Most of Eira’s clothes were gone.","Her side had never been crowded. She rarely bought anything for herself, though she had never hesitated to order new suits, shirts, or ties for him. Now only a few outfits remained.","Alpha Sebastian stared at the empty hangers.","When had she moved everything?","He tried to remember the last time he had seen her packing and came up blank.","The thought bothered him more than it should have.","In the shower, the shampoo bottle ran dry in his hand. The body wash was almost empty too, and there were no replacements in the cabinet.","He stood beneath the water, irritated at first.","Then the truth hit him.","Before their marriage, household staff had managed things like supplies and laundry. After Eira moved in, she had quietly taken over. The cabinets stayed full. His clothes appeared clean and pressed. Meals were ready when he came home.","He had never asked how any of it happened.","He had simply expected it.","Eira had been gone for less than a week, and the house was already beginning to show it.","Alpha Sebastian shut off the water, grabbed a towel, and checked his phone.","No missed calls. No messages.","He opened their conversation and typed: Come home. We need to talk.","He stared at the words, then added: I’m waiting for you.","---","Eira woke with a pounding headache and reached for her phone.","Alpha Sebastian’s message filled the screen.","[Come home. We need to talk. I’m waiting for you.]","She stared at it.","Early in their marriage, those words would have sent her running back. She had wanted a family so badly that she spent four years taking care of Alpha Sebastian and the Hales, hoping they would finally treat her like one of their own.","They never did.","Now come home was just another order from a man who had never loved her.","Eira dismissed the message without replying.","Another one waited beneath it.","Martin: Please check in when you can. Mrs. Thorne is worried. Alpha Hale stopped by late last night looking for you.","Eira frowned.","Alpha Sebastian had taken Serena to the gala, denied Eira was his wife, and then shown up at the Thorne house after midnight?","The man had more nerve than common sense.","She let Martin know she was safe, then looked around.","She was in Lila’s bed. Her shoes sat neatly beside it, and a blanket covered her legs.","Her memory returned in ugly little pieces.","The wine. Lila passing out. The phone call.","Alpha Killian’s voice.","Then came the tears, the spicy chicken, and the Band-Aid she had asked him to put on her broken heart.","Eira closed her eyes.","She had called him Mom.","Mrs. Thorne was always in bed early. There was no way she had shown up at a wine bar after midnight.","Which meant Eira had cried all over her boss and called him Mom to his face.","\"Great,\" she muttered. \"I can never go back to work.\"","She swung her legs over the side of the bed, only to step on someone’s fingers.","\"Ow!\"","Lila shot upright from the floor, her hair sticking out in every direction.","\"What the hell?\"","Eira jerked her foot back. \"Lila? Why are you sleeping on the floor?\"","Lila squinted at her. \"Why are you stepping on people before coffee?\"","The two women stared at each other.","\"Wait.\" Lila rubbed her face. \"Why am I on the floor?”","Eira blinked. \"Maybe I kicked you off the bed.\"","\"You don’t sound sorry.\"","\"I don’t remember doing it.\"","A knock sounded against the bedroom door.","\"It’s eleven twenty-three,\" Alpha Killian called through the door. \"Get up. Lunch is ready.\"","Lila’s eyes widened. \"Why is my brother in my apartment?\"","\"He picked us up from the bar.\"","Lila went pale. \"Crap. He knows I own the place.\"","\"He already knew.\"","\"Of course he did.\"","She dragged herself to her feet.","Eira pushed aside the blanket and froze.","A small Band-Aid was stuck to the front of her gown, right over her heart.","So that part had been real too.","Lila noticed it and grinned.","\"Did my brother put that there?\"","\"I was drunk.\"","\"That wasn’t my question.\"","Eira peeled it from her dress and set it on the nightstand.","\"We’re never discussing this.\"","\"Sure. We’ll discuss it after coffee.\"","Lila opened the door. The smell of coffee and food drifted in from the living room.","Alpha Killian sat on the couch with a tablet.","\"I need something for Eira to wear,\" Lila said.","Alpha Killian handed her a shopping bag from beside him.","\"Already taken care of.\"","Inside was a white sweater dress and an olive cashmere coat, both new.","Lila glanced at the labels, then looked at her brother with a knowing smile.","Then she removed the tags and carried the clothes back to the bedroom.","Eira assumed they belonged to her and took them into the bathroom to change.","The white dress fell to mid-calf, and the olive coat fit perfectly through the shoulders and sleeves.","Too perfectly.","Lila was shorter than Eira. These clothes had clearly not come from her closet.","When Eira stepped into the living room, both siblings looked up.","The soft white dress made her look elegant without seeming formal, while the green coat brought out the warmth of her eyes.","Lila’s face lit up. \"My brother has excellent taste.\"","In clothes, at least. She kept the rest of the thought to herself.","So Alpha Killian had chosen the outfit.","Eira walked over to him.","\"Thank you, Alpha Killian. What do I owe you?\"","Lila recognized the brands. The outfit was expensive, but nowhere near outrageous by Sterling standards.","She opened her mouth to answer.","\"Call it a hundred grand,\" Alpha Killian said.","Lila’s jaw dropped.","Eira stared at him. \"For a dress and a coat?\"","\"You’re the one who insisted on paying me back.\" Alpha Killian leaned into the couch, looking far too pleased with himself. \"Still interested, Ms. Crawford?\""]},{"number":50,"title":"Chapter 50 The Chili Chicken","paragraphs":["Eira slipped off the coat.","\"If I can’t afford it, I’ll return it.\"","Alpha Killian stared at her, clearly not expecting her to call his bluff.","Lila quickly pulled the coat back over Eira’s shoulders.","\"He’s messing with you. The outfit was about four grand, not a hundred thousand.\"","Eira took out her phone and sent Alpha Killian the money.","His phone buzzed.","\"You haven’t even gotten your first paycheck from Sterling.\"","\"I have my own money.\"","He sent it back.","Eira’s phone buzzed a second later. She met his eyes.","\"Keep it, or I’ll take everything off and leave it on your couch.\"","Lila nearly spit out her coffee.","Alpha Killian’s gaze swept over Eira’s dress before returning to her face.","\"You might want to rephrase that.\"","\"You know what I meant.\"","\"Do I?\"","A hint of amusement flashed in his eyes.","Eira sent the money again.","\"Send it back one more time and you’ll find out.\"","For a moment, neither of them looked away.","Then Alpha Killian slipped his phone into his pocket without returning the money.","\"Fine.\"","--","The three of them sat down, and Lila opened the takeout containers.","Sandwiches, fries, salads, and soup covered most of the table. Then she lifted the lid from the last box.","The chicken inside was deep red, served over white bread with pickles on the side.","Lila leaned back.","\"Please tell me that isn’t the kind that comes with a waiver.\"","Alpha Killian slid the box toward Eira.","\"You asked for Nashville hot chicken.\"","Eira looked at him.","Last night, she had asked for two things. A Band-Aid for her heart and chicken hot enough to burn for two days.","He had remembered both.","She picked up a piece and took a bite.","The heat hit immediately. Her eyes watered, but the familiar mix of spice, fried chicken, and pickles made her smile.","Lila stared at her.","\"Your face is turning red.\"","\"It’s supposed to.\"","\"That cannot be enjoyable.\"","\"It is if you do it right.\"","Alpha Killian pushed a glass of milk toward Eira without a word.","She took it, still smiling.","\"I haven’t had this in four years.\"","Lila’s expression changed. \"Why not?\"","\"Sebastian gets heartburn, and his family hates spicy food. Dinner was always about what they wanted.\"","\"So you never ordered something for yourself?\"","Eira shrugged. \"After a while, it felt easier not to.\"","Lila looked disgusted.","\"They couldn’t let you have one meal you liked?\"","Eira glanced at the chicken.","\"They never thought to ask.\"","Alpha Killian’s face remained calm, but his jaw tightened.","Lila pushed the entire box closer to Eira.","\"Then it’s all yours. Alpha Sebastian can enjoy his sad, unseasoned chicken without you.\"","A laugh escaped Eira.","\"Gladly.\"","After lunch, Alpha Killian checked his watch.","\"We need to leave soon.\"","\"I’ll be ready,\" Eira said.","Lila suddenly frowned. \"Wait. You’re missing an earring.\"","Eira touched her bare earlobe and blinked. \"Huh. You’re right.\"","\"It’s probably in the bedroom. I’ll go check.\"","\"I’m coming with you.\"","The two women headed back to the bedroom and started looking around. Alpha Killian stayed behind to call a cleaning service and have someone come take care of the house.","When he slipped his phone back into his pocket, his fingers brushed against something hard.","He pulled it out.","Eira’s missing pearl earring lay in his palm.","It must have come loose when he carried her upstairs the night before.","The white pearl caught the afternoon light, giving off a soft, warm glow.","\"Found it,\" he called.","Eira and Lila stopped searching and came out of the bedroom.","Lila let out a breath. \"Thank God. I thought it was gone for good.\"","\"Thanks, Alpha Killian.\" Eira reached for the earring.","He raised his hand just out of reach.","Eira looked up at him, clearly confused.","Before she could ask what he was doing, Alpha Killian stepped closer and leaned down. His free hand reached toward her ear.","The moment his warm fingers brushed her skin, Eira flinched as if he had touched her with a hot iron.","She quickly snatched the earring from his hand and took a step to the side. Tilting her head, she put it back on herself.","\"There. I’ve got it. You don’t have to fuss over me.\"","Alpha Killian’s eyes grew darker for a brief moment. Then he lowered his hand as if nothing had happened.","\"Right.\"","He turned and walked toward the door.","Just before he stepped outside, he stopped and glanced back.","\"You coming?\"","Lila pointed at herself. \"Me?\"","Alpha Killian’s gaze shifted to Eira.","\"Eira is. We’re heading to the office.\"","Lila nodded toward the door. \"Go with him. His driver’s downstairs, and I have a thesis draft that’s already way past due.\"","Eira picked up the bag holding her gown and followed Alpha Killian into the hall. She was still wearing the white sneakers he had bought with the outfit.","--","Sterling Industries Headquarters","Employees began to notice the moment Alpha Killian and Eira crossed the lobby together.","He wore a dark tailored suit and polished Oxfords. She wore a white sweater dress, an olive cashmere coat, and clean white sneakers.","They should have looked mismatched.","Somehow, they did not.","A few heads turned. By the time they reached the elevators, the office grapevine was already warming up.","Eira noticed none of it. She had removed her colored contacts that morning and forgotten her glasses, leaving every face across the lobby a blur.","She headed for the employee elevators, but Alpha Killian caught her lightly by the elbow.","\"This way.\"","He guided her toward the private elevator.","\"I can take the regular one.\"","\"I know.\"","\"Then why am I going with you?\"","The doors opened.","\"Because this one is faster.\"","Eira gave him a skeptical look but stepped inside.","When they reached the executive floor, the assistants were professional enough not to react.","\"Good afternoon, Alpha Sterling.\"","\"Hey, Eira.\"","Alpha Killian walked into his office, and Miles followed him with a folder.","\"Silix Institute sent over an invitation-only RFP for the Sovereign Processor Initiative.\"","Alpha Killian opened the folder. \"The project they shut down years ago?\"","\"It’s active again. Federal funding, limited bidders, and strict security rules. Nothing has been announced yet.\"","\"Who else was invited?\"","\"We don’t have the full list, but I narrowed the likely competition down to ten companies.\"","Miles handed him a page.","Hale Group was near the top.","Alpha Killian tapped the folder.","\"Put a proposal team together today. I want the first draft on my desk by the end of the week.\"","\"I’ll get started.\" Miles paused. \"Should I bring Natalie, Kate, and Eira onto the team?\"","Alpha Killian looked up.","\"You’re asking about Eira.\"","\"She knows the field better than anyone else in this office.\"","Alpha Killian glanced through the glass wall. Eira was already at her desk, focused on her computer.","\"Ask her.\"","Miles smiled. That was all the approval he needed.","He returned to the outer office.","\"Eira, we just received an RFP for a major processor project. We’d like you on the proposal team.\"","She looked up. \"What’s the deadline?\"","\"Less than a month. You’d help with the technical proposal and join us for the final presentation.\"","\"I can’t.\"","Miles had not expected such a quick answer.","\"Why not?\"","\"I’m leaving Sterling.\"","\"You’re really going through with that?\"","Eira frowned. \"I submitted my notice days ago. Has HR not finished the paperwork?\"","Miles opened his mouth.","Then closed it.","The paperwork WAS being processed.","But Alpha Killian wasn’t letting it go through."]}]);
